answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279383} :answer-field/id #uuid "2e3e03e8-92a5-53c7-a1d7-ee9ae71efd68" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280917}] :question/id #uuid "9939f92b-9874-5d18-8b59-989570a881e7" :question/math-academy-id "q-162704" :question/problem "The matrix\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}a & 0 \\\\ 0 & b\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nrepresents the linear transformation that acts on a vector in ${R}^{2}$ as follows (in the order given):\n\n- It rotates the vector  $\\pi $ radians counterclockwise about the origin, then\n\n- stretches the result by a scale factor of $3$ parallel to the $x$-axis, and finally\n\n- reflects the result about the $x$-axis.\n\nWhat is the value of $a+b?$" :question/worked-solution "Let $P$ be the matrix that represents the rotation, $Q$ be the matrix that represents the stretching, and $R$ be the matrix that represents the reflection. These are given by the following elementary transformation matrices:\n\n$$\nP=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix},\\,Q=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,R=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nHence, the combined transformation can be represented by the matrix $RQP:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}RQP & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n$a+b=(-3)+1=-2.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186294914 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "65f299c3-044f-53f9-9efd-1a75489d9c12" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293355}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293355} :answer-field/id #uuid "38557ea6-a941-53d5-ab27-d2cf1e182630" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294121} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b8063972-aa60-5850-8d9b-83413e801657" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293650}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293650} :answer-field/id #uuid "7612eaa3-abb1-5b87-aafb-5864ac585c30" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294346} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ada60079-680b-5daf-aae5-637e1beadf12" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293612}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293612} :answer-field/id #uuid "e08f3467-ddb5-5989-a241-06db663b56d5" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294714}] :question/id #uuid "61d89e52-8793-52b7-9d83-7ebf0e38a50e" :question/math-academy-id "q-277771" :question/problem "Construct the matrix $T$ of the linear transformation $T$ that acts on a vector in ${R}^{2}$ as follows (in the order given):\n\n- It rotates the vector by $\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ radians **clockwise** about the origin, then\n\n- stretches the result by a scale factor of $5$ parallel to the $x$-axis, and finally\n\n- shears the result with a shear factor of $3$ parallel to the $x$-axis.\n\n|  |  | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $T=\\,\\,$ |  |  |  |  |\n|  |  | {{field-3}} | $0$ |  |" :question/worked-solution "Let $P$ be the matrix that represents the rotation, $Q$ be the matrix that represents the stretching, and $R$ be the matrix that represents the shearing. These are given by the following elementary transformation matrices:\n\n$$\nP=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,Q=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,R=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\,\\,\n$$\n\nHence, the combined transformation can be represented by the matrix $RQP:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T & =RQP \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 5 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186295099 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5f63f39f-e2a6-5449-bb80-0b73a8ab8a0f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293319}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293319} :answer-field/id #uuid "6f1b3e24-b5ee-5844-b554-b8c0d2e758f0" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294319} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7f3e2d9f-9890-53fe-a9b0-85c439006e92" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293444}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293444} :answer-field/id #uuid "8d4fa2e7-0eea-5f2a-a4d6-f19099868e6e" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294436} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "677e8536-0131-5b01-88a3-2efa9d0b29c6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293362}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293362} :answer-field/id #uuid "c9995bf8-703c-5afe-94