7592186481379 :question/id #uuid "66f9559c-8f7e-590d-8f2d-e6935f863326"} :step/id #uuid "ffca9ec5-be0b-5330-9fd1-5e439c5ad7d1" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186481461}}] :activity/title "The Column Space of a Matrix" :activity/type {:db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186480732}] :db/id #edb/ref 17592186050656 :topic/knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119810 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119621 :question/id #uuid "244793f6-41c3-5920-9264-bec32cda9c9c" :question/math-academy-id "e-4807" :question/problem "The matrix $B$ and the vector $\\mathbf{b}$ are given below. \nDetermine if $\\mathbf{b} \\in \\textrm{Col}(B).$ \nIn the affirmative case, find the values of $x_1$ and $x_2,$ where $x_1$ and $x_2$ are the real numbers such that $\\mathbf{b}=x_1\\mathbf{b}_1+x_2\\mathbf{b}_2,$ and $\\mathbf{b}_1,$ $\\mathbf{b}_2$ are the respective columns of $B.$\n\n![](images/a6/a65747aa11107acc9a05df83473ed0208c23818953b16771b608ec4f572dc7ca.svg)" :question/worked-solution "In order to determine whether $\\mathbf{b}$ lies in $\\textrm{Col}(B),$ we need to check if the equation $B\\mathbf{x}=\\mathbf{b}$ is consistent. So, let's find the row echelon form of the augmented matrix $[B \\,|\\, \\mathbf{b}]$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[B\\,|\\,b] & =\\begin{bmatrix}5 & -2 & 7 \\\\ 15 & -6 & 21 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}5 & -2 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & ↔{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}5 & -2 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the system\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}5{x}_{1}-2{x}_{2} &=7 \\\\ {x}_{2} &=0 \\\\ 0 &=0.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFrom the third equation, we get the true statement $0=0.$ So the system is equivalent to the following:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}5{x}_{1}-2{x}_{2} &=7 \\\\ {x}_{2} &=0\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get $x_2=0.$ Substituting into the first equation gives $x_1=\\dfrac 7 5.$ \n\nSince we have a solution, the equation $B\\mathbf{x}=\\mathbf{b}$ is consistent, which implies that $\\mathbf{b}\\in\\textrm{Col}(B).$\n\nMoreover, there is exactly one solution, so we have exactly one way to write $\\mathbf{b}$ as a linear combination of $\\mathbf{b}_1$ and $\\mathbf{b}_2\\mathbin{:}$\n![](images/8a/8a35321d3a29ee86c5af54e23dabd8d3ac93bf7831981507dff3e501796f96a7.svg)"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5c8e217c-252d-529f-a810-84787e2ee886" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120313 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "907cc16b-4753-575b-b5ba-b46432765efe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118018} {:answer/id #uuid "d11a9abd-92ca-59ae-9aaa-21023336d51d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118019} {:answer/id #uuid "1b7a8c24-da3d-5a69-a785-b262d211b5b6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118020} {:answer/id #uuid "4db10aa6-a706-5fb0-9811-1880e036ef4a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "b ∉ Col(B)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118021} {:answer/id #uuid "7ba605d8-ec38-503b-9282-1543f79efe9c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118022}] :answer-field/id #uuid "74a717fc-cda7-5f15-b43f-23aa21022fe0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118017}] :question/id #uuid "d240f240-a11b-5de3-8d2a-b9852522828d" :question/math-academy-id "q-34258" :question/problem "The matrix $B$ and the vector $b$ are given below. Determine if $b ∈ Col(B)$. In the affirmative case, find the value of $x_{1} \\cdot x_{2}$, where $x_{1}$ and $x_{2}$ are real numbers such that $b = x_{1}b_{1} + x_{2}b_{2}$, and $b_{1}$, $b_{2}$ are the respective columns of $B$.\n\n$B = \\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 \\\\ 4 & 0\\end{bmatrix}, b = \\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120339 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8bf8b71d-a371-5f81-974e-5142050a5df6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118164} {:answer/id #uuid "b384fbdd-d0d7-5c26-b21c-91c01ea1c932" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118165} {:answer/id #uuid "b463d47c-d91c-5c81-9a10-4d392e054e3d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118166} {:answer/id #uuid "65cc9e17-49dc-56a5-b839-9140f465bbd4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118168} {:answer/id #uuid "a4e728bc-a0d7-5941-ae7e-43acb5d00189" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "b\\notin \\text{Col}(H)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186429994}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "b\\notin \\text{Col}(H)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186429994} :answer-field/id #uuid "2d44952a-9dfe-5d35-aaf5-e2dab2e19171" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118163}] :question/id #uuid "d584fac7-0bb8-5af7-99db-3f6ce440972c" :question/math-academy-id "q-34499" :question/problem "The matrix $H$ and the vector $b$ are given below. Determine if $b\\in \\text{Col}(H).$ In the affirmative case, find the value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}$, where ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ are real numbers such that $b={x}_{1}{h}_{1}+{x}_{2}{h}_{2},$ and ${h}_{1},$ ${h}_{2}$ are the respective columns of $H.$\n\n$$\nH=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix},\\,b=\\begin{bmatrix}7 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "In order to determine whether $b$ lies in $\\text{Col}(H),$ we need to check if the equation $Hx=b$ is consistent. So, let's find the row echelon form of the augmented matrix $[H\\,|\\,b]$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[H\\,|\\,b] & =\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 4 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 2\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-2{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 4 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the system\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-{x}_{1}+4{x}_{2} &=7 \\\\ {x}_{2} &=2 \\\\ 0 &=-2.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFrom the third equation, we get the false statement $0=-2.$ \n\nTherefore, the system is inconsistent, which implies that $b\\notin \\text{Col}(H).$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186247182 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "04899405-c481-5f48-aab9-064ce77af89b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244352} {:answer/id #uuid "196e46c8-7360-5f30-873f-7c67c6d5d13a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "b\\notin \\text{Col}(A)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244540} {:answer/id #uuid "1f36d8fd-b667-56e3-9388-2d063fbe71ca" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244585} {:answer/id #uuid "2d659fe5-c014-5f11-bb9b-5044efcd71b1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244721} {:answer/id #uuid "56218cbe-0674-5eb6-9e5f-532434e4091a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245072}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "b\\notin \\text{Col}(A)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244540} :answer-field/id #uuid "879a804e-d385-58e0-80a6-7a7ed5c2339e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246783}] :question/id #uuid "a7d58e5a-0e86-5643-9b08-933ce7a04992" :question/math-academy-id "q-110938" :question/problem "The matrix $A$ and the vector $b$ are given below. Determine if $b\\in \\text{Col}(A).$ In the affirmative case, find the value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}$, where ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ are real numbers such that $b={x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2},$ and ${a}_{1},$ ${a}_{2}$ are the respective columns of $A.$\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ \\,\\,-2 & \\,\\,-2 \\\\ \\,\\,-1 & \\,\\,-1\\end{bmatrix},\\,b=\\begin{bmatrix}\\,\\,-4 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "In order to determine whether $b$ lies in $\\text{Col}(A),$ we need to check if the equation $Ax=b$ is consistent. So, let's find the row echelon form of the augmented matrix $[A\\,|\\,b]$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[A\\,|\\,b] & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & \\,\\,-4 \\\\ \\,\\,-2 & \\,\\,-2 & 2 \\\\ \\,\\,-1 & \\,\\,-1 & 2\\end{bmatrix} &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\ {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+{R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & \\,\\,-4 \\\\ 0 & \\,\\,2 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2\\end{bmatrix} &  & {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}-\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & \\,\\,-4 \\\\ 0 & \\,\\,2 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the system\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2} &=-4 \\\\ 2{x}_{2} &=-6 \\\\ 0 &=1.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFrom the third equation, we get the false statement $0=1.$ \n\nTherefore, the system is inconsistent, which implies that $b\\notin \\text{Col}(A).$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186247183 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "64681709-1170-5f03-bea9-39e2b3e08575" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245196} {:answer/id #uuid "a0926f48-6f17-50d3-9063-207c796ae337" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245743} {:answer/id #uuid "ce6ac71b-167b-59ce-a9a5-a3eba31e72bd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246158} {:answer/id #uuid "d22a5c7d-7f39-58dc-99f7-e2e02fb8f361" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "b\\notin \\text{Col}(M)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246183} {:answer/id #uuid "e4fc31d7-a002-5bb5-984c-f7279ca052e0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246344}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245743} :answer-field/id #uuid "7ab43adf-8d8a-5661-838f-2a606959c5c0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246760}] :question/id #uuid "e29736ad-5a46-5b75-954a-5f47e0d7b1bc" :question/math-academy-id "q-110955" :question/problem "The matrix $M$ and the vector $b$ are given below. Determine if $b\\in \\text{Col}(M).$ In the affirmative case, find the value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2},$ where ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ are real numbers such that $b={x}_{1}{m}_{1}+{x}_{2}{m}_{2},$ and ${m}_{1},$  ${m}_{2}$ are the respective columns of $M.$ \n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & -1 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{bmatrix},\\,b=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 8 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "In order to determine whether $b$ lies in $\\text{Col}(M),$ we need to check if the equation $Mx=b$ is consistent. So, let's find the row echelon form of the augmented matrix $[M\\,|\\,b]$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[M\\,|\\,b] & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 8 \\\\ -1 & -1 & -4\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 8 \\\\ -1 & -1 & -4\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -4\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the system\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2} &=0 \\\\ -4{x}_{2} &=8 \\\\ 0 &=0.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation we get ${x}_{2}=-2.$ Substituting into the first equation gives  ${x}_{1}=6.$  \n\nSince we have a solution, the equation $Mx=b$ is consistent, which implies that $b\\in \\text{Col}(M).$\n\nMoreover, there is exactly one solution, so we have exactly one way to write $b$ as a linear combination of ${m}_{1}$ and ${m}_{2}:$\n\n$$\n{{\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 8 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{b}=6\\cdot {{\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{{m}_{1}}+(-2)\\cdot {{\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{{m}_{2}}\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, we get ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}=6(-2)=-12.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186247185 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5afd7296-0e41-5a52-8705-c7c0fbb42d4b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245110} {:answer/id #uuid "6432d9a5-cb06-5009-a488-f5f4aca2c370" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245195} {:answer/id #uuid "64fbeade-a556-57de-b9d8-c66b01089ebc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "b\\notin \\text{Col}(C)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245207} {:answer/id #uuid "a639644e-969e-5af1-8ddb-b741ba91a374" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245801} {:answer/id #uuid "e2c696c1-ce2c-55ff-89ef-065b9ea5e562" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246330}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "b\\notin \\text{Col}(C)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245207} :answer-field/id #uuid "bf8f671a-ae62-58c4-8bc0-0e675cc16311" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246892}] :question/id #uuid "7005444a-a247-5177-8b52-a944d472324a" :question/math-academy-id "q-110969" :question/problem "The matrix $C$ and the vector $b$ are given below. Determine if $b\\in \\text{Col}(C).$ In the affirmative case, find the value of ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}$, where ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ are real numbers such that $b={x}_{1}{c}_{1}+{x}_{2}{c}_{2},$ and ${c}_{1},$ ${c}_{2}$ are the respective columns of $C.$\n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -3\\end{bmatrix},\\,b=\\begin{bmatrix}9 \\\\ -15\\end{bmatrix}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "In order to determine whether $b$ lies in $\\text{Col}(C),$ we need to check if the equation $Cx=b$ is consistent. So, let's find the row echelon form of the augmented matrix $[C\\,|\\,b]$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[C\\,|\\,b] & =\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 1 & 9 \\\\ 3 & -3 & -15\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 1 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 12\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the system\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-{x}_{1}+{x}_{2} &=9 \\\\ 0 &=12.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get the false statement $0=12.$  \n\nTherefore, the system is inconsistent, which implies that $b\\notin \\text{Col}(C).$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186317417 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0a344ba4-7e9e-5133-8de4-ea4267e37212" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315170} {:answer/id #uuid "284f1cde-92ac-5c9f-a53e-63c45a513d5d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315350} {:answer/id #uuid "45825ac5-30cd-54cc-ad99-cb6dba8de5ca" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315521} {:answer/id #uuid "866fa2db-6a19-55cd-b98a-1606663103a6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "b\\notin \\text{Col}(F)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315873} {:answer/id #uuid "a1fac86c-323a-53ee-b319-af0b21358d9d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316031}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315350} :answer-field/id #uuid "a5a252af-653f-5519-a11a-ff0d918098e6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316931}] :question/id #uuid "0d0936ed-b5bf-5b20-a019-8454c54094c7" :question/math-academy-id "q-34366" :question/problem "The matrix $F$ and the vector $b$ are given below. Determine if $b\\in \\text{Col}(F).$ In the affirmative case, find the value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}$, where ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ are real numbers such that $b={x}_{1}{f}_{1}+{x}_{2}{f}_{2},$ and ${f}_{1},$  ${f}_{2}$ are the respective columns of $F.$\n\n$$\nF=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,b=\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "In order to determine whether $b$ lies in $\\text{Col}(F),$ we need to check if the equation $Fx=b$ is consistent. So, let's find the row echelon form of the augmented matrix $[F\\,|\\,b]$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[F\\,|\\,b] & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 5 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 7 & -14\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the system\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-2{x}_{2} &=5 \\\\ 7{x}_{2} &=-14.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation we get ${x}_{2}=-2.$ Substituting into the first equation gives  ${x}_{1}=1.$ \n\nSince we have a solution, the equation $Fx=b$ is consistent, which implies that $b\\in \\text{Col}(F).$\n\nMoreover, there is exactly one solution, so we have exactly one way to write $b$ as a linear combination of ${f}_{1}$ and ${f}_{2}:$\n\n$$\n{{\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{b}=1\\cdot {{\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{{f}_{1}}+(-2)\\cdot {{\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{{f}_{2}}\n$$\n\nFinally, we get ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}=1\\cdot (-2)=-2.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186342180 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "07220986-b6ef-5f2b-9d70-55d9d3cdf5c4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339189} {:answer/id #uuid "768f93e4-f2dc-58f6-9248-6843bc28585f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340184} {:answer/id #uuid "7b551627-5521-5602-9e00-01d66a6247d3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "b\\notin \\text{Col}(A)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340233} {:answer/id #uuid "d2ca2c76-34f1-5f50-ba00-3df45686c200" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340994} {:answer/id #uuid "f098d80e-fa77-5c14-87cb-a76611b99c40" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341245}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "b\\notin \\text{Col}(A)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340233} :answer-field/id #uuid "13717f75-08cc-5654-aa63-2873767d2941" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341412}] :question/id #uuid "efbc99ee-782d-5cfc-bd9c-e3ca79e0d68e" :question/math-academy-id "q-74198" :question/problem "The matrix $A$ and the vector $b$ are given below. Determine if $b\\in \\text{Col}(A).$ In the affirmative case, find the value of ${x}_{1}-{x}_{2}$, where ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ are real numbers such that $b={x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2},$ and ${a}_{1},$ ${a}_{2}$ are the respective columns of $A.$\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & -5 \\\\ 1 & -3\\end{bmatrix},\\,b=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "In order to determine whether $b$ lies in $\\text{Col}(A),$ we need to check if the equation $Ax=b$ is consistent. So, let's find the row echelon form of the augmented matrix $[A\\,|\\,b]$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[A\\,|\\,b] & =\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -5 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -3 & -1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 1 & -3 & -1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the system\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2} &=2 \\\\ {x}_{2} &=5 \\\\ 0 &=1.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFrom the third equation, we get the false statement $0=1.$ \n\nTherefore, the system is inconsistent, which implies that $b\\notin \\text{Col}(A).$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408163 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0e09706e-9bae-5390-a4c8-454afb7bdba9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186408138} {:answer/id #uuid "310c69d2-39ad-5656-a9df-2348bfbcfc3d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186408139} {:answer/id #uuid "676b432f-8135-5f04-aa24-f35508646c7d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186408145} {:answer/id #uuid "c34b20ad-6cc0-5427-81db-158ceccf5944" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186408152} {:answer/id #uuid "cdc0656a-82ba-50bd-b21a-9c93190c767d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "b\\notin \\text{Col}(K)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186408153}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "b\\notin \\text{Col}(K)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186408153} :answer-field/id #uuid "529d609f-c755-5038-98fc-5e940ab6a79a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186408159}] :question/id #uuid "0a92dafd-51fb-510b-93ec-662d06afe5a3" :question/math-academy-id "q-34503" :question/problem "The matrix $K$ and the vector $b$ are given below. Determine if $b\\in \\text{Col}(K).$ In the affirmative case, find the value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2},$ where ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ are real numbers such that $b={x}_{1}{k}_{1}+{x}_{2}{k}_{2},$ and ${k}_{1},$ ${k}_{2}$ are the respective columns of $K.$\n\n$$\nK=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -8 \\\\ 0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,b=\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "In order to determine whether $b$ lies in $\\text{Col}(K),$ we need to check if the equation $Kx=b$ is consistent. So, let's find the row echelon form of the augmented matrix $[K\\,|\\,b]$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[K\\,|\\,b] & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -8 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 4\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -8 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 2\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-4{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -8 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -18\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the system\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}-8{x}_{2} &=4 \\\\ {x}_{2} &=5 \\\\ 0 &=-18.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFrom the third equation, we get the false statement $0=-18.$ \n\nTherefore, the system is inconsistent, which implies that $b\\notin \\text{Col}(K).$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186430002 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "093c0e17-b9d7-5361-b0f1-495edfe1ed11" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186429981} {:answer/id #uuid "6c9a2490-6ff3-538d-b8fc-292a428032fc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186429988} {:answer/id #uuid "9a2ac221-6a8f-511f-bdab-4c58f95296f8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186429992} {:answer/id #uuid "abc883cc-1645-5165-aa94-e26727b22c02" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "b\\notin \\text{Col}(K)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186429995} {:answer/id #uuid "cc637fff-6c90-5ccd-9438-8fa331c95ad6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186429996}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "b\\notin \\text{Col}(K)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186429995} :answer-field/id #uuid "fa9df3d7-3177-5d86-afd1-6157ae9530cb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186429999}] :question/id #uuid "fa3eae70-d536-57c6-818d-d88d2dc98925" :question/math-academy-id "q-110965" :question/problem "The matrix $K$ and the vector $b$ are given below. Determine if $b\\in \\text{Col}(K).$ In the affirmative case, find the value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2},$ where ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ are real numbers such that $b={x}_{1}{k}_{1}+{x}_{2}{k}_{2},$ and ${k}_{1},$ ${k}_{2}$ are the respective columns of $K.$\n\n$$\nK=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{bmatrix},\\,b=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "In order to determine whether $b$ lies in $\\text{Col}(K),$ we need to check if the equation $Kx=b$ is consistent. So, let's find the row echelon form of the augmented matrix $[K\\,|\\,b]$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[K\\,|\\,b] & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{2}+{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the system\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-2{x}_{1}+{x}_{2} &=2 \\\\ 2{x}_{2} &=0 \\\\ 0 &=3.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFrom the third equation, we get the false statement $0=3.$  \n\nTherefore, the system is inconsistent, which implies that $b\\notin \\text{Col}(K).$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Determining if a Vector is in the Column Space of a Matrix"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119811 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119622 :question/id #uuid "12f222d8-5563-544a-8154-fb1f9406b231" :question/math-academy-id "e-4808" :question/problem "The matrix $C$ and the vector $\\mathbf{b}$ are given below. Determine if $\\mathbf{b} \\in \\textrm{Col}(C).$ In affirmative case, find the value of $x_1 \\cdot x_2 \\cdot x_3$, where $x_1$, $x_2$, and $x_3$ are real numbers such that $\\mathbf{b}=x_1\\mathbf{c}_1+x_2\\mathbf{c}_3+x_3\\mathbf{c}_3,$ and $\\mathbf{c}_1,$ $\\mathbf{c}_2,$ and $\\mathbf{c}_3$ are the respective columns of $C.$\n\n![](images/02/027332c5a5bdb14913d297e71bc2ac2ae8f846976c1bc3c0c4c569997dcd5b01.svg)" :question/worked-solution "In order to determine whether $\\mathbf{b}$ lies in $\\textrm{Col}(C),$ we need to check if the equation $C\\mathbf{x}=\\mathbf{b}$ is consistent. So, let's find the row echelon form of the augmented matrix $[C \\,|\\, \\mathbf{b}]$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[C\\,|\\,b] & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 4 & 5 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 0 & -4 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 1 & 4\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 4 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 4 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 1 & 4\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 4 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 4 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5 & 5\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the system\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+4{x}_{3} &=5 \\\\ 3{x}_{2}+4{x}_{3} &=1 \\\\ 5{x}_{3} &=5.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFrom the third equation, we get $x_3=1$. Substituting into the second equation gives \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{x}_{2}+4(1) & =1 \\\\ 3{x}_{2} & =-3 \\\\ {x}_{2} & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, from the first equation, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =5-{x}_{2}-4{x}_{3} \\\\  & =5-(-1)-4(1) \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince we have a solution, the equation $C\\mathbf{x}=\\mathbf{b}$ is consistent, which implies that $\\mathbf{b}\\in\\textrm{Col}(C).$ \n\nMoreover, there is exactly one solution, so we have exactly one way to write $\\mathbf{b}$ as a linear combination of $\\mathbf{c}_1,$ $\\mathbf{c}_2,$ and $\\mathbf{c}_3\\mathbin{:}$\n![](images/4c/4cccd67d5e043d72e0b6949543883e6187d9ef807b7a470146628cbadf7eead7.svg)\n\nFinally, we get $x_1 \\cdot x_2 \\cdot x_3 = 2 \\cdot (-1) \\cdot 1 = -2$."} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "87dc8398-fb5c-564b-a796-db15ff30d72c" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120314 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a11faf82-bd4b-5c21-a04c-3f6e36d5cd40" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118024} {:answer/id #uuid "a920e021-eeb6-5640-bcc8-6d23e6afec05" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118025} {:answer/id #uuid "14651a2e-216c-52fe-ae0a-7d78664efba6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118026} {:answer/id #uuid "4d413782-be19-5bb6-b18c-6a054f9da757" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "b ∉ Col(C)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118027} {:answer/id #uuid "7ade2344-cc5f-5cd0-a5f6-2404d16af604" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118028}] :answer-field/id #uuid "1d909091-a2b7-59a5-b8c2-d2c77b10d744" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118023}] :question/id #uuid "754364b6-d225-59c9-ac68-b2c45892e451" :question/math-academy-id "q-34260" :question/problem "The matrix $C$ and the vector $b$ are given below.\nDetermine if $b ∈ Col(C)$.\nIn the affirmative case, find the value of $x_{1} \\cdot x_{2} \\cdot x_{3}$, where $x_{1}, x_{2}$ and $x_{3}$ are real numbers such that $b = x_{1}c_{1} + x_{2}c_{2} + x_{3}c_{3}$, and $c_{1}$, $c_{2}$, and $c_{3}$ are the respective columns of $C$.\n\n$C = \\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 1 & -3 & 0\\end{bmatrix}, b = \\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix}$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120515 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "29da3f11-da36-5a93-b224-a37d8e81c149" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339496} {:answer/id #uuid "3bda870a-e008-5fcd-8921-d9b462b64cc3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339661} {:answer/id #uuid "7e4be675-e0f6-5007-9ea2-797607fdb517" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340267} {:answer/id #uuid "8b618a4a-be3e-5ad8-9ca8-4d4102c61425" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "b\\notin \\text{Col}(E)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340377} {:answer/id #uuid "ff722db2-a186-58ef-bd64-b656f5cfdc12" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341381}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "b\\notin \\text{Col}(E)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340377} :answer-field/id #uuid "1e2b899c-9539-5cca-acdc-bf68af89936a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341434}] :question/id #uuid "0554a363-6902-58e6-8a93-41a3bab0a0ff" :question/math-academy-id "q-74080" :question/problem "The matrix $E$ and the vector $b$ are given below.\nDetermine if $b\\in \\text{Col}(E).$ \nIn the affirmative case, find the value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}\\cdot {x}_{3}\\cdot {x}_{4}$, where ${x}_{1}$, ${x}_{2}$, ${x}_{3}$, and ${x}_{4}$ are real numbers such that $b={x}_{1}{e}_{1}+{x}_{2}{e}_{2}+{x}_{3}{e}_{3}+{x}_{4}{e}_{4},$ and ${e}_{1}$, ${e}_{2}$, ${e}_{3}$, and ${e}_{4}$ are respective columns of $E.$\n\n$$\nE=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -4 & 7 & 1 \\\\ 4 & -16 & 28 & 4 \\\\ 1 & -3 & 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix},\\,b=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 7 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "In order to determine whether $b$ lies in $\\text{Col}(E),$ we need to check if the equation $Ex=b$ is consistent. So, let's find the row echelon form of the augmented matrix $[E\\,|\\,b]$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[E\\,|\\,b] & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -4 & 7 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 4 & -16 & 28 & 4 & 7 \\\\ 1 & -3 & 0 & -1 & 0\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-4){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -4 & 7 & 1 & 2 \\\\ \\text{ }0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -3 & 0 & -1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the system\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-4{x}_{2}+7{x}_{3}+{x}_{4} &=2 \\\\ 0 &=-1 \\\\ {x}_{1}-3{x}_{2}-{x}_{4} &=0.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get a false statement $0=-1.$ Therefore, the system is inconsistent, and we conclude that $b\\notin \\text{Col}(E).$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186247191 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "05dd1857-2985-546b-9aba-fc98eb855d94" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244360} {:answer/id #uuid "20acb5fc-d805-5850-bfb0-2f0f05d25203" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244601} {:answer/id #uuid "2c4cd3b2-1f4e-53be-932d-e0f8f8127322" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244706} {:answer/id #uuid "3940ebec-c39e-553c-b6aa-55bd069457ed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244821} {:answer/id #uuid "7d7b3c15-cef9-5072-800b-26138a27eae4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245415}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244706} :answer-field/id #uuid "2ca7504e-b5bc-5c05-8761-5692c93d71f4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246619}] :question/id #uuid "b861c0c2-25f8-5f54-84a3-3dea6f60c30d" :question/math-academy-id "q-110982" :question/problem "The matrix $C$ and the vector $b$ are given below.\nDetermine if $b\\in \\text{Col}(C).$ \nIn the affirmative case, find the value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}\\cdot {x}_{3}$, where ${x}_{1},{x}_{2}$ and ${x}_{3}$ are real numbers such that $b={x}_{1}{c}_{1}+{x}_{2}{c}_{2}+{x}_{3}{c}_{3},$ and ${c}_{1}$, ${c}_{2}$, and ${c}_{3}$ are the respective columns of $C.$\n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,b=\\begin{bmatrix}-8 \\\\ -12 \\\\ -6\\end{bmatrix}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "In order to determine whether $b$ lies in $\\text{Col}(C),$ we need to check if the equation $Cx=b$ is consistent. So, let's find the row echelon form of the augmented matrix $[C\\,|\\,b]$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[C\\,|\\,b] & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 & 3 & -8 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -1 & -12 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 0 & -6\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 & 3 & -8 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -1 & -12 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 3 & -14\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 & 3 & -8 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -1 & -12 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5 & 10\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the system\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3} &=-8 \\\\ 2{x}_{2}-{x}_{3} &=-12 \\\\ 5{x}_{3} &=10.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFrom the third equation, we get ${x}_{3}=2.$ Substituting it into the second equation gives \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{2}-(2) & =-12 \\\\ {x}_{2} & =-5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, from the first equation, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =-8-3{x}_{2}-3{x}_{3} \\\\  & =-8-3(-5)-3(2) \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince we have a solution, the equation $Cx=b$ is consistent, which implies that $b\\in \\text{Col}(C).$ \n\nMoreover, there is exactly one solution, so we have exactly one way to write $b$ as a linear combination of ${c}_{1},$ ${c}_{2},$ and ${c}_{3}:$\n\n$$\n{{\\begin{bmatrix}-8 \\\\ -12 \\\\ -6\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{b}=1\\cdot {{\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{{c}_{1}}+(-5)\\cdot {{\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{{c}_{2}}+2\\cdot {{\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{{c}_{3}}\n$$\n\nFinally, we get ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}\\cdot {x}_{3}=1\\cdot (-5)\\cdot 2=-10.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186247192 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "002a439c-2842-5d1e-810b-2b542db359a5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "23" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244300} {:answer/id #uuid "4a011f6f-d375-50d7-836f-0e8d861b17ef" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "34" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244972} {:answer/id #uuid "9c0862b1-6730-52c0-8a62-ebdf2153695c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245696} {:answer/id #uuid "d9c7d7ac-06eb-5406-babb-1ac034337f43" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246251} {:answer/id #uuid "f85aa94a-4629-5d8f-91a0-d23d6462a022" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246499}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245696} :answer-field/id #uuid "48377fc5-ae90-5f13-8b71-0384837c02f6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246664}] :question/id #uuid "85af463a-fe91-5600-aaed-1c1e9aea31cb" :question/math-academy-id "q-110983" :question/problem "The matrix $M$ and the vector $b$ are given below.\nDetermine if $b\\in \\text{Col}(M).$ \nIn the affirmative case, find the value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}\\cdot {x}_{3}$, where ${x}_{1},{x}_{2}$ and ${x}_{3}$ are real numbers such that $b={x}_{1}{m}_{1}+{x}_{2}{m}_{2}+{x}_{3}{m}_{3},$ and ${m}_{1}$, ${m}_{2}$, and ${m}_{3}$ are the respective columns of $M.$\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -2 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,b=\\begin{bmatrix}9 \\\\ -6 \\\\ 8\\end{bmatrix}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "In order to determine whether $b$ lies in $\\text{Col}(M),$ we need to check if the equation $Mx=b$ is consistent. So, let's find the row echelon form of the augmented matrix $[M\\,|\\,b]$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[M\\,|\\,b] & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 0 & 9 \\\\ 2 & -2 & 4 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 8\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 0 & 9 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 4 & -24 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 8\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & ↔{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 0 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 8 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 4 & -24\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+4{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 0 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4 & 8\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the system\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+{x}_{2} &=9 \\\\ {x}_{2} &=8 \\\\ {x}_{3} &=2.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFinally, from the first equation, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+(8) & =9 \\\\ {x}_{1} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSince we have a solution, the equation $Mx=b$ is consistent, which implies that $b\\in \\text{Col}(M).$ \n\nMoreover, there is exactly one solution, so we have exactly one way to write $b$ as a linear combination of ${m}_{1},$ ${m}_{2},$ and ${m}_{3}:$\n\n$$\n{{\\begin{bmatrix}9 \\\\ -6 \\\\ 8\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{b}=1\\cdot {{\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{{m}_{1}}+8\\cdot {{\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{{m}_{2}}+2\\cdot {{\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{{m}_{3}}\n$$\n\nFinally, we get ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}\\cdot {x}_{3}=1\\cdot 8\\cdot 2=16.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186247198 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "166e5731-ef25-53ae-954b-a5d68566d3fb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244521} {:answer/id #uuid "9d50769c-b616-5e35-8235-04c2208dd3bd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "30" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245713} {:answer/id #uuid "cda94c8f-e9f9-5c21-8e75-1697ea682454" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246147} {:answer/id #uuid "df7db205-d92a-5e90-88b8-4fbdc783ef1c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "b\\notin \\text{Col}(E)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246295} {:answer/id #uuid "ffde8a56-754f-5068-ad96-07cdb70d4eed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "48" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246548}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "b\\notin \\text{Col}(E)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246295} :answer-field/id #uuid "6c804267-f2e6-568e-98f1-93b1fb6a2f71" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246736}] :question/id #uuid "e1365590-672c-5168-b364-de16fc710406" :question/math-academy-id "q-111050" :question/problem "The matrix $E$ and the vector $b$ are given below.\nDetermine if $b\\in \\text{Col}(E).$ \nIn the affirmative case, find the value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}\\cdot {x}_{3}\\cdot {x}_{4}$, where ${x}_{1}$, ${x}_{2}$, ${x}_{3}$, and ${x}_{4}$ are real numbers such that $b={x}_{1}{e}_{1}+{x}_{2}{e}_{2}+{x}_{3}{e}_{3}+{x}_{4}{e}_{4},$ and ${e}_{1}$, ${e}_{2}$, ${e}_{3}$, and ${e}_{4}$ are respective columns of $E.$\n\n$$\nE=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 5 & -15 & 0 & 20 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 7 & -1\\end{bmatrix},\\,b=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ -8 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "In order to determine whether $b$ lies in $\\text{Col}(E),$ we need to check if the equation $Ex=b$ is consistent. So, let's find the row echelon form of the augmented matrix $[E\\,|\\,b]$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[E\\,|\\,b] & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3 & 0 & 4 & -2 \\\\ 5 & -15 & 0 & 20 & -8 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 7 & -1 & 6\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-5){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3 & 0 & 4 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 7 & -1 & 6\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the system\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-3{x}_{2}+4{x}_{4} &=-2 \\\\ 0 &=2 \\\\ {x}_{2}+7{x}_{3}-{x}_{4} &=6\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get a false statement $0=2.$ Therefore, the system is inconsistent, and we conclude that $b\\notin \\text{Col}(E).$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186247199 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "24560bed-2a72-5a6d-8ff8-d2299393dfac" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "50" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244634} {:answer/id #uuid "2c956e55-8139-5fd0-8d29-b8ea83e541a5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244711} {:answer/id #uuid "419dc35e-ce15-59ce-b655-6acbeaa9c1a8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244888} {:answer/id #uuid "495d4449-e670-5f2d-9723-6a86e6ce2c3e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244966} {:answer/id #uuid "5cea6f1c-7c7c-59f1-9899-41ad06a3a42b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "b\\notin \\text{Col}(M)." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245133}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "b\\notin \\text{Col}(M)." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245133} :answer-field/id #uuid "54bdb17f-9390-5096-9cce-7c0cc5a71903" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246695}] :question/id #uuid "31975565-2751-59e9-bd8b-c536e60e66d3" :question/math-academy-id "q-111053" :question/problem "The matrix $M$ and the vector $b$ are given below.\nDetermine if $b\\in \\text{Col}(M).$ \nIn the affirmative case, find the value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}\\cdot {x}_{3}\\cdot {x}_{4}$, where ${x}_{1}$, ${x}_{2}$, ${x}_{3}$, and ${x}_{4}$ are real numbers such that $b={x}_{1}{m}_{1}+{x}_{2}{m}_{2}+{x}_{3}{m}_{3}+{x}_{4}{m}_{4},$ and ${m}_{1}$, ${m}_{2}$, ${m}_{3}$, and ${m}_{4}$ are respective columns of $M.$\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & -2 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 0 & -1 \\\\ -3 & -3 & 6 & -12\\end{bmatrix},\\,b=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "In order to determine whether $b$ lies in $\\text{Col}(M),$ we need to check if the equation $Mx=b$ is consistent. So, let's find the row echelon form of the augmented matrix $[M\\,|\\,b]$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[M\\,|\\,b] & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & -2 & 4 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 0 & -1 & 1 \\\\ -3 & -3 & 6 & -12 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & -2 & 4 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 0 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & -8\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the system\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}-2{x}_{3}+4{x}_{4} &=-3 \\\\ {x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}-{x}_{4} &=1 \\\\ 0 &=8.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFrom the third equation, we get a false statement $0=8.$ Therefore, the system is inconsistent, and we conclude that $b\\notin \\text{Col}(M).$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186317403 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "70aa6d55-c534-5b07-a3c7-473cdbe543ac" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315752} {:answer/id #uuid "8e797cc1-2116-5eb4-9f1f-6dbcd8106246" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315917} {:answer/id #uuid "924aae74-4eba-5a47-bf45-0b952819441a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "b\\notin \\text{Col}(D)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315935} {:answer/id #uuid "a7572984-ad61-550b-9248-f8429f133d04" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316059} {:answer/id #uuid "ee30e00a-d305-5260-a85c-343d5a4ed9d3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316442}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "b\\notin \\text{Col}(D)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315935} :answer-field/id #uuid "2113ec9e-911b-5430-8a70-aed3b47d67bc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316625}] :question/id #uuid "d1232415-f101-5f93-96ed-3610c46ba358" :question/math-academy-id "q-34346" :question/problem "The matrix $D$ and the vector $b$ are given below.\nDetermine if $b\\in \\text{Col}(D).$ \nIn the affirmative case, find the value of ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}+{x}_{4}$, where ${x}_{1}$, ${x}_{2}$, ${x}_{3}$, and ${x}_{4}$ are real numbers such that $b={x}_{1}{d}_{1}+{x}_{2}{d}_{2}+{x}_{3}{d}_{3}+{x}_{4}{d}_{4},$ and ${d}_{1}$, ${d}_{2}$, ${d}_{3}$, and ${d}_{4}$ are respective columns of $D.$\n\n$$\nD=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & 4 & 7 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 4 & 0 & 6 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 3 & -1\\end{bmatrix},\\,b=\\begin{bmatrix}11 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "In order to determine whether $b$ lies in $\\text{Col}(D),$ we need to check if the equation $Dx=b$ is consistent. So, let's find the row echelon form of the augmented matrix $[D\\,|\\,b]$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[D\\,|\\,b] & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & 4 & 7 & 11 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 3 & -1 & -2 \\\\ 4 & 0 & 6 & -2 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 3 & -1 & 7\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-2){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & 4 & 7 & 11 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 3 & -1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 9 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 3 & -1 & 7\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the system\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}+4{x}_{3}+7{x}_{4} &=11 \\\\ 2{x}_{1}+3{x}_{3}-{x}_{4} &=-2 \\\\ 0 &=9 \\\\ {x}_{1}+3{x}_{3}-{x}_{4} &=7.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFrom the third equation, we get a false statement $0=9.$ Therefore, the system is inconsistent, and we conclude that $b\\notin \\text{Col}(D).$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186317416 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0137f4f1-683a-5532-86ac-a58609ac6c5a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315122} {:answer/id #uuid "36dddeda-f4aa-5342-a56d-21d473781fec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "b\\notin \\text{Col}(E)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315436} {:answer/id #uuid "40a90e71-399a-5c76-8a51-5bf7d89f38b6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315490} {:answer/id #uuid "5eed2d17-3d66-58ef-b9ca-d14343adcf9f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315652} {:answer/id #uuid "fe5e2b84-4825-5e40-b36f-66a99eaaf9f8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316542}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "b\\notin \\text{Col}(E)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315436} :answer-field/id #uuid "4285fcd0-9fe1-5d74-91ff-bd01e5c9f93a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316697}] :question/id #uuid "d2325a17-fb51-5bea-98a4-12b407e10918" :question/math-academy-id "q-34364" :question/problem "The matrix $E$ and the vector $b$ are given below.\nDetermine if $b\\in \\text{Col}(E).$ \nIn the affirmative case, find the value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}\\cdot {x}_{3}\\cdot {x}_{4}$, where ${x}_{1}$, ${x}_{2}$, ${x}_{3}$, and ${x}_{4}$ are real numbers such that $b={x}_{1}{e}_{1}+{x}_{2}{e}_{2}+{x}_{3}{e}_{3}+{x}_{4}{e}_{4},$ and ${e}_{1}$, ${e}_{2}$, ${e}_{3}$, and ${e}_{4}$ are respective columns of $E.$\n\n$$\nE=\\begin{bmatrix}8 & -2 & 5 & 1 \\\\ 16 & -4 & 10 & 2 \\\\ 11 & -3 & 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix},\\,b=\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "In order to determine whether $b$ lies in $\\text{Col}(E),$ we need to check if the equation $Ex=b$ is consistent. So, let's find the row echelon form of the augmented matrix $[E\\,|\\,b]$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[E\\,|\\,b] & =\\begin{bmatrix}8 & -2 & 5 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 16 & -4 & 10 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 11 & -3 & 0 & -1 & 0\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}8 & -2 & 5 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & -9 \\\\ 11 & -3 & 0 & -1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the system\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}8{x}_{1}-2{x}_{2}+5{x}_{3}+{x}_{4} &=4 \\\\ 0 &=-9 \\\\ 11{x}_{1}-3{x}_{2}-{x}_{4} &=0.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get a false statement $0=-9.$ Therefore, the system is inconsistent, and we conclude that $b\\notin \\text{Col}(E).$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186342189 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "51465e72-8fe6-56d7-b118-66fc195903ac" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339873} {:answer/id #uuid "5f7f00e0-de0d-5136-8d20-7baf7199c74a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339976} {:answer/id #uuid "7b0b0da7-c66e-5d54-b708-00e47e0f720e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340229} {:answer/id #uuid "7f9de184-3104-5023-bfd8-46750d413c68" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340275} {:answer/id #uuid "e48af61b-5d78-571c-a99d-e895740fda4b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341150}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340229} :answer-field/id #uuid "32bb0ceb-025b-5bfd-a775-2c1301a72219" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341473}] :question/id #uuid "3ab37f17-4ea0-5e43-8d25-5328ba6ba1aa" :question/math-academy-id "q-74223" :question/problem "The matrix $M$ and the vector $b$ are given below.\nDetermine if $b\\in \\text{Col}(M).$ \nIn the affirmative case, find the value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}\\cdot {x}_{3}$, where ${x}_{1},{x}_{2}$ and ${x}_{3}$ are real numbers such that $b={x}_{1}{m}_{1}+{x}_{2}{m}_{2}+{x}_{3}{m}_{3},$ and ${m}_{1}$, ${m}_{2}$, and ${m}_{3}$ are the respective columns of $M.$\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 & -5 \\\\ 2 & 1 & -4 \\\\ 6 & 0 & -13\\end{bmatrix},\\,b=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 16\\end{bmatrix}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "In order to determine whether $b$ lies in $\\text{Col}(M),$ we need to check if the equation $Mx=b$ is consistent. So, let's find the row echelon form of the augmented matrix $[M\\,|\\,b]$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[M\\,|\\,b] & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 & -5 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1 & -4 & 1 \\\\ 6 & 0 & -13 & 16\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 & -5 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 6 & 0 & -13 & 16\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 & -5 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 2 & 10\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & ↔{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 & -5 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 2 & 10 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the system\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}-5{x}_{3} &=2 \\\\ -3{x}_{2}+2{x}_{3} &=10 \\\\ {x}_{3} &=-1.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFrom the third equation, we get ${x}_{3}=-1.$ Substituting it into the second equation gives \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-3{x}_{2}+2(-1) & =10 \\\\ -3{x}_{2}-2 & =10 \\\\ -3{x}_{2} & =12 \\\\ {x}_{2} & =-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, from the first equation, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}+(-4)-5(-1) & =2 \\\\ 2{x}_{1}+1 & =2 \\\\ 2{x}_{1} & =1 \\\\ {x}_{1} & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince we have a solution, the equation $Mx=b$ is consistent, which implies that $b\\in \\text{Col}(M).$ \n\nMoreover, there is exactly one solution, so we have exactly one way to write $b$ as a linear combination of ${m}_{1},$ ${m}_{2},$ and ${m}_{3}:$\n\n$$\n{{\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 16\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{b}=\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot {{\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{{m}_{1}}+(-4)\\cdot {{\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{{m}_{2}}+(-1)\\cdot {{\\begin{bmatrix}-5 \\\\ -4 \\\\ -13\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{{m}_{3}}\n$$\n\nFinally, we get ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}\\cdot {x}_{3}=\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot (-4)\\cdot (-1)=2.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408162 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "78645ea0-f8bd-5f81-bf27-fac8caad6e9c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "b\\notin \\text{Col}(D)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186408146} {:answer/id #uuid "7acd09aa-e693-553d-8659-2bccadf0cd4f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "36" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186408147} {:answer/id #uuid "a9c33b38-1f8c-54fe-a1a1-31dc93958a1a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186408148} {:answer/id #uuid "af5fd598-f27a-56c8-bd28-250a38b55ee9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186408149} {:answer/id #uuid "b263cee4-a3ad-5f42-875f-5cc9d7a2c77d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186408150}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "b\\notin \\text{Col}(D)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186408146} :answer-field/id #uuid "9a398de2-1cab-5e15-93f0-5e8dde00197f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186408160}] :question/id #uuid "06040e86-0928-550a-a9a4-3db2bc9e2e31" :question/math-academy-id "q-111046" :question/problem "The matrix $D$ and the vector $b$ are given below.\nDetermine if $b\\in \\text{Col}(D).$ \nIn the affirmative case, find the value of ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}+{x}_{4}$, where ${x}_{1}$, ${x}_{2}$, ${x}_{3}$, and ${x}_{4}$ are real numbers such that $b={x}_{1}{d}_{1}+{x}_{2}{d}_{2}+{x}_{3}{d}_{3}+{x}_{4}{d}_{4},$ and ${d}_{1}$, ${d}_{2}$, ${d}_{3}$, and ${d}_{4}$ are respective columns of $D.$\n\n$$\nD=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & -3 & -2 \\\\ -2 & -2 & 6 & 4 \\\\ 2 & 2 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 6 & 5 & -1\\end{bmatrix},\\,b=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 8 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "In order to determine whether $b$ lies in $\\text{Col}(D),$ we need to check if the equation $Dx=b$ is consistent. So, let's find the row echelon form of the augmented matrix $[D\\,|\\,b]$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[D\\,|\\,b] & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & -3 & -2 & 1 \\\\ -2 & -2 & 6 & 4 & 4 \\\\ 2 & 2 & 1 & 1 & 8 \\\\ 1 & 6 & 5 & -1 & 6\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+2{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & -3 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 6 \\\\ 2 & 2 & 1 & 1 & 8 \\\\ 1 & 6 & 5 & -1 & 6\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the system\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}-3{x}_{3}-2{x}_{4} &=1 \\\\ 0 &=6 \\\\ 2{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}+{x}_{4} &=-8 \\\\ {x}_{1}+6{x}_{2}+5{x}_{3}-{x}_{4} &=6.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFrom the  second equation, we get a false statement $0=6.$ Therefore, the system is inconsistent, and we conclude that $b\\notin \\text{Col}(D).$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408164 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4543a202-3ccc-5eab-b11e-9acd9fffb1d8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186408141} {:answer/id #uuid "47160327-abda-5117-a3f6-534dafb7314d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186408142} {:answer/id #uuid "49158a7c-f7b1-5aa2-a277-f0ac8325fc0b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186408143} {:answer/id #uuid "56c7eda1-7b63-555c-9f5f-b736c9f51e0b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186408144} {:answer/id #uuid "fa79a18c-e454-55de-b1b8-442bf38cb930" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186408155}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186408141} :answer-field/id #uuid "eb0ebf0b-554c-514b-a72c-5d817e3dd52a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186408161}] :question/id #uuid "2009c6af-efbe-5caf-a9f3-bb999b290a0f" :question/math-academy-id "q-74221" :question/problem "The matrix $A$ and the vector $b$ are given below.\nDetermine if $b\\in \\text{Col}(A).$ \nIn the affirmative case, find the value of ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}$, where ${x}_{1},{x}_{2}$ and ${x}_{3}$ are real numbers such that $b={x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3},$ and ${a}_{1}$, ${a}_{2}$, and ${a}_{3}$ are the respective columns of $A.$\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -4 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 10 & -7 \\\\ 3 & -12 & 10\\end{bmatrix},\\,b=\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ 11 \\\\ -13\\end{bmatrix}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "In order to determine whether $b$ lies in $\\text{Col}(A),$ we need to check if the equation $Ax=b$ is consistent. So, let's find the row echelon form of the augmented matrix $[A\\,|\\,b]$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[A\\,|\\,b] & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -4 & 3 & -4 \\\\ -2 & 10 & -7 & 11 \\\\ 3 & -12 & 10 & -13\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -4 & 3 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 3 & -12 & 10 & -13\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -4 & 3 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the system\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-4{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3} &=-4 \\\\ 2{x}_{2}-{x}_{3} &=3 \\\\ {x}_{3} &=-1.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFrom the third equation, we get ${x}_{3}=-1.$ Substituting it into the second equation gives \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{2}-(-1) & =3 \\\\ 2{x}_{2} & =2 \\\\ {x}_{2} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, from the first equation, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =-4+4{x}_{2}-3{x}_{3} \\\\  & =-4+4(1)-3(-1) \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince we have a solution, the equation $Ax=b$ is consistent, which implies that $b\\in \\text{Col}(A).$ \n\nMoreover, there is exactly one solution, so we have exactly one way to write $b$ as a linear combination of ${a}_{1},$ ${a}_{2},$ and ${a}_{3}:$\n\n$$\n{{\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ 11 \\\\ -13\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{b}=3\\cdot {{\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{{a}_{1}}+1\\cdot {{\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ 10 \\\\ -12\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{{a}_{2}}+(-1)\\cdot {{\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -7 \\\\ 10\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{{a}_{3}}\n$$\n\nFinally, we get ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}=3+1+(-1)=3.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186424110 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "158fd3b6-b42a-5e9e-b83d-ee548a2f6fa5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "b\\notin \\text{Col}(A)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424104} {:answer/id #uuid "791e7d26-9d1f-5803-b774-f6e2358c4273" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424105} {:answer/id #uuid "a421f5cb-8c63-56cc-847e-0b15d335d55e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424106} {:answer/id #uuid "dab0c485-45d4-554d-af12-2b22d279fbd1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{15}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424107} {:answer/id #uuid "ed81c627-15f5-5ac5-9a83-8720033ed743" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424108}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424105} :answer-field/id #uuid "a69e7526-7c64-51e8-b0ec-23524a78858f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424109}] :question/id #uuid "b249af0d-2baa-56c1-b03f-659223bf8b34" :question/math-academy-id "q-35572" :question/problem "The matrix $A$ and the vector $b$ are given below.\nDetermine if $b\\in \\text{Col}(A).$ \nIn the affirmative case, find the value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}\\cdot {x}_{3}$, where ${x}_{1},{x}_{2}$ and ${x}_{3}$ are real numbers such that $b={x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3},$ and ${a}_{1}$, ${a}_{2}$, and ${a}_{3}$ are the respective columns of $A.$\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 & -8 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 4 \\\\ 2 & 0 & -4\\end{bmatrix},\\,b=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "In order to determine whether $b$ lies in $\\text{Col}(A),$ we need to check if the equation $Ax=b$ is consistent. So, let's find the row echelon form of the augmented matrix $[A\\,|\\,b]$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[A\\,|\\,b] & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 & -8 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 4 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 0 & -4 & 2\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 & -8 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 4 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -6 & 12 & 6\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-6){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 & -8 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 4 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -12 & -6\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the system\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2}-8{x}_{3} &=-2 \\\\ -{x}_{2}+4{x}_{3} &=2 \\\\ -12{x}_{3} &=-6.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFrom the third equation, we get ${x}_{3}=\\frac{1}{2}.$ Substituting it into the second equation gives \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-{x}_{2}+4(\\frac{1}{2}) & =2 \\\\ -{x}_{2}+2 & =2 \\\\ {x}_{2} & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, from the first equation, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+3(0)-8(\\frac{1}{2}) & =-2 \\\\ {x}_{1}-4 & =-2 \\\\ {x}_{1} & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince we have a solution, the equation $Ax=b$ is consistent, which implies that $b\\in \\text{Col}(A).$ \n\nMoreover, there is exactly one solution, so we have exactly one way to write $b$ as a linear combination of ${a}_{1},$ ${a}_{2},$ and ${a}_{3}:$\n\n$$\n{{\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{b}=2\\cdot {{\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{{a}_{1}}+0\\cdot {{\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{{a}_{2}}+\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot {{\\begin{bmatrix}-8 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{{a}_{3}}\n$$\n\nFinally, we get ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}\\cdot {x}_{3}=2\\cdot 0\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}=0.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186430001 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1828c4ca-eb5d-5389-aec1-1f80b5436666" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "b\\notin \\text{Col}(C)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186429982} {:answer/id #uuid "33644fcb-15fc-5a07-8b9c-fcbe4057fb01" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186429985} {:answer/id #uuid "3bb23460-0309-50b0-9f56-6030ff2b9177" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-30" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186429986} {:answer/id #uuid "7c7bc9e5-99a0-5450-9994-235495344319" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-28" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186429989} {:answer/id #uuid "9c2abbdd-3e2c-554e-8306-7b4a584274a0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186429993}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-30" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186429986} :answer-field/id #uuid "936859a3-a75e-5199-89df-699c1acfd3b4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186429998}] :question/id #uuid "6e653566-d375-5ee1-b745-3dfd829381b0" :question/math-academy-id "q-111042" :question/problem "The matrix $C$ and the vector $b$ are given below.\nDetermine if $b\\in \\text{Col}(C).$ \nIn the affirmative case, find the value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}\\cdot {x}_{3}$, where ${x}_{1},{x}_{2}$ and ${x}_{3}$ are real numbers such that $b={x}_{1}{c}_{1}+{x}_{2}{c}_{2}+{x}_{3}{c}_{3},$ and ${c}_{1}$, ${c}_{2}$, and ${c}_{3}$ are the respective columns of $C.$\n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 1 & -4 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 3\\end{bmatrix},\\,b=\\begin{bmatrix}9 \\\\ -8 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "In order to determine whether $b$ lies in $\\text{Col}(C),$ we need to check if the equation $Cx=b$ is consistent. So, let's find the row echelon form of the augmented matrix $[C\\,|\\,b]$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[C\\,|\\,b] & =\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 1 & -4 & 9 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 0 & -8 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 3 & 5\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & ↔{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 3 & 5 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 0 & -8 \\\\ 4 & 1 & -4 & 9\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 3 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 3 & -3 \\\\ 4 & 1 & -4 & 9\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-4{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 3 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 3 & -3 \\\\ 0 & -7 & -16 & -11\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(\\frac{7}{3}){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 3 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 3 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -9 & -18\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the system\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3} &=5 \\\\ 3{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3} &=-3 \\\\ -9{x}_{3} &=-18.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFrom the third equation, we get ${x}_{3}=2.$ Substituting it into the second equation gives \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{x}_{2}+3(2) & =-3 \\\\ {x}_{2} & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, from the first equation, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =5-2{x}_{2}-3{x}_{3} \\\\  & =5-2(-3)-3(2) \\\\  & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince we have a solution, the equation $Cx=b$ is consistent, which implies that $b\\in \\text{Col}(C).$ \n\nMoreover, there is exactly one solution, so we have exactly one way to write $b$ as a linear combination of ${c}_{1},$ ${c}_{2},$ and ${c}_{3}:$\n\n$$\n{{\\begin{bmatrix}9 \\\\ -8 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{b}=5\\cdot {{\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{{c}_{1}}+(-3)\\cdot {{\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{{c}_{2}}+2\\cdot {{\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{{c}_{3}}\n$$\n\nFinally, we get ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}\\cdot {x}_{3}=5\\cdot (-3)\\cdot 2=-30.$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Determining if a Vector Is in the Column Space of a Larger Matrix"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119855 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119670 :question/id #uuid "b6d52e39-a8a0-5048-80a1-a342a2617e0f" :question/math-academy-id "e-6208" :question/problem "Consider the matrix given by ![](images/fd/fdab914fd2a1013caf1d02dc692df697f4c61f61b3aeba6166b471f3833e7811.svg) Determine the value of $k$ for which the vector ![](images/a8/a8acb2b133143150953e861f13e7b9797756c557800b67ca0334a88d26eb3cc9.svg) belongs to $\\textrm{Col}(A).$" :question/worked-solution "If $\\mathbf{b}$ lies in $\\textrm{Col}(A),$ then the equation $A\\mathbf{x}=\\mathbf{b}$ must be consistent. So, let's find the row echelon form of the augmented matrix $[A \\,|\\, \\mathbf{b}]$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[A\\,|\\,b] & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 10 \\\\ 3 & -2 & -2 \\\\ 5 & -1 & 2+k\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 10 \\\\ 0 & -8 & -32 \\\\ 5 & -1 & 2+k\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-5{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 10 \\\\ 0 & -8 & -32 \\\\ 0 & -11 & k-48\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :=\\frac{1}{8}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 10 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -11 & k-48\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+11{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 10 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & k-4\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the system\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2} &=10 \\\\ {x}_{2} &=4 \\\\ 0 &=k-4.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nIn order for this system to be consistent, we require $0=k-4,$ which means that $k=4.$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a557ee8d-51a9-5387-a28c-67ffefed55b4" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120397 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "826165fc-f641-5f1a-94bd-36d5b21a3d8c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118497} {:answer/id #uuid "b7e517cb-5c7c-5901-9fc8-4d62de0ffa87" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118498} {:answer/id #uuid "d09a578d-a4f8-5169-ae0b-3f5e8801df37" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118499} {:answer/id #uuid "1c9f1214-ef5c-5445-be91-c3914d8f5865" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118500} {:answer/id #uuid "20d99621-dbd7-526e-832d-85b050d0bddd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118501}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118500} :answer-field/id #uuid "82d94d35-2966-563a-ae36-53ee87337d99" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118496}] :question/id #uuid "573bc22a-fac9-5364-8084-060fccb61060" :question/math-academy-id "q-35567" :question/problem "Consider the matrix given by $A=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 8 \\\\ -2 & -11 \\\\ 1 & 6\\end{bmatrix}.$ Determine the value of $k$ for which the vector $b=\\begin{bmatrix}14 \\\\ -15 \\\\ k+5\\end{bmatrix}$ belongs to $\\text{Col}(A).$" :question/worked-solution "If $b$ lies in $\\text{Col}(A),$ then the equation $Ax=b$ must be consistent. So, let's find the row echelon form of the augmented matrix $[A\\,|\\,b]$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[A\\,|\\,b] & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 8 & 14 \\\\ -2 & -11 & -15 \\\\ 1 & 6 & k+5\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 6 & k+5 \\\\ -2 & -11 & -15 \\\\ 3 & 8 & 14\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 6 & k+5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2k-5 \\\\ 3 & 8 & 14\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 6 & k+5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2k-5 \\\\ 0 & -10 & -3k-1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+10{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 6 & k+5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2k-5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 17k-51\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the system\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+6{x}_{2} &=k+5 \\\\ {x}_{2} &=2k-5 \\\\ 0 &=17k-51.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nIn order for this system to be consistent, we require $0=17k-51,$ which means that $k=3.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120398 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a486a0ed-b6cb-5e19-8b3c-df26f94eca01" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118503} {:answer/id #uuid "bd29e70f-c8bb-5c3d-8d7a-cd8c4f21ec0c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118504} {:answer/id #uuid "c8c4668f-aef9-5b0e-9c4a-93fd4e302226" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118505} {:answer/id #uuid "ec11e6d6-5f22-5f3a-a260-ce7ea2d3051a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118506} {:answer/id #uuid "4e1e33dc-82e3-500c-8be5-73571081c164" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118507}] :answer-field/id #uuid "6477fdd2-6beb-5cff-8663-1cbfcd609ceb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118502}] :question/id #uuid "c8ba3063-b478-52ac-8cfa-9cd555352654" :question/math-academy-id "q-35568" :question/problem "Consider the matrix given by $A = \\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 \\\\ 2 & -2 \\\\ 5 & -8\\end{bmatrix}$. Determine the value of $k$ for which the vector $b = \\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ k\\end{bmatrix}$ belongs to $Col(A)$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186247187 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0a518ba8-7e5a-5330-a0c3-7dc41839b810" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244403} {:answer/id #uuid "5ecfbb60-c0e1-5b3d-9917-a4be218ee6c7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245148} {:answer/id #uuid "8780347e-20b1-500b-b92b-04a826db56f8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245508} {:answer/id #uuid "95e86051-0f00-5126-8951-6fe196a1942b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245629} {:answer/id #uuid "d1547734-6592-5e4a-b0b1-e78a453cd79f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "28" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246177}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245148} :answer-field/id #uuid "d88358ca-e18a-5086-839c-b003b585540c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246933}] :question/id #uuid "c4554bbb-8fca-5283-8d92-22082ac865b7" :question/math-academy-id "q-110974" :question/problem "Consider the matrix given by $A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3 \\\\ -1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -2\\end{bmatrix}.$ Determine the value of $k$ for which the vector $b=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -5 \\\\ k\\end{bmatrix}$ belongs to $\\text{Col}(A).$" :question/worked-solution "If $b$ lies in $\\text{Col}(A),$ then the equation $Ax=b$ must be consistent. So, let's find the row echelon form of the augmented matrix $[A\\,|\\,b]$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[A\\,|\\,b] & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 1 & -5 \\\\ 2 & -2 & k\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -4 \\\\ 2 & -2 & k\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 4 & k-2\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+2{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & k-10\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the system\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-3{x}_{2} &=1 \\\\ -2{x}_{2} &=-4 \\\\ 0 &=k-10.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nIn order for this system to be consistent, we require $0=k-10,$ which means that $k=10.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186247188 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "00d59342-4323-5d82-9ec6-79c204057d31" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244314} {:answer/id #uuid "25ee40ae-0e2d-5af2-8558-d3c593a1061c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244650} {:answer/id #uuid "30b1ab51-7901-51a8-aedd-d5577a9bac09" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244749} {:answer/id #uuid "79b84a02-a53e-5fed-bab0-07b2cd9e849c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245385} {:answer/id #uuid "ab3edfe6-975a-59a6-b885-6bacccb3ff7f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245843}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245843} :answer-field/id #uuid "59a3d3af-9c4a-5e27-9c86-8143c023a969" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246706}] :question/id #uuid "48a49394-e77c-53ab-a102-d1b40a287f43" :question/math-academy-id "q-110976" :question/problem "Consider the matrix given by $L=\\begin{bmatrix}8 & -1 \\\\ 2 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.$ Determine the value of $k$ for which the vector $b=\\begin{bmatrix}7k-1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}$ belongs to $\\text{Col}(L).$" :question/worked-solution "If $b$ lies in $\\text{Col}(L),$ then the equation $Lx=b$ must be consistent. So, let's find the row echelon form of the augmented matrix $[L\\,|\\,b]$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[L\\,|\\,b] & =\\begin{bmatrix}8 & -1 & 7k-1 \\\\ 2 & -2 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 3\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & -2 & -2 \\\\ 8 & -1 & 7k-1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -4 & -8 \\\\ 8 & -1 & 7k-1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-8{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -4 & -8 \\\\ 0 & -9 & 7k-25\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :=(-\\frac{1}{4}){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -9 & 7k-25\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+9{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 7k-7\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the system\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+{x}_{2} &=3 \\\\ {x}_{2} &=2 \\\\ 0 &=7k-7.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nIn order for this system to be consistent, we require $0=7k-7,$ which means that $k=1.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186247190 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "145aaf0d-c740-5655-ae4b-ab7ab839b1d1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-32" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244501} {:answer/id #uuid "3645011b-7dde-5f85-8688-666dc335211c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "40" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244793} {:answer/id #uuid "44437890-b323-5fd5-97ac-226cbb6e05ad" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-21" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244911} {:answer/id #uuid "cf93de62-0950-5d23-bca5-5947fd12768b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-31" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246164} {:answer/id #uuid "e1ef9d00-cd89-59a6-b58c-1a2654314dc9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-23" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246324}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-21" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244911} :answer-field/id #uuid "aa5a0518-d9be-57b6-b478-a86c9d9b1ec7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246855}] :question/id #uuid "fc664822-35fb-5c04-9e53-89dd85c50706" :question/math-academy-id "q-110979" :question/problem "Consider the matrix given by $A=\\begin{bmatrix}-5 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.$ Determine the value of $k$ for which the vector $b=\\begin{bmatrix}-8 \\\\ k \\\\ 10\\end{bmatrix}$ belongs to $\\text{Col}(A).$" :question/worked-solution "If $b$ lies in $\\text{Col}(A),$ then the equation $Ax=b$ must be consistent. So, let's find the row echelon form of the augmented matrix $[A\\,|\\,b]$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[A\\,|\\,b] & =\\begin{bmatrix}-5 & 1 & -8 \\\\ 0 & -3 & k \\\\ 1 & 1 & 10\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 10 \\\\ 0 & -3 & k \\\\ -5 & 1 & -8\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+5{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 10 \\\\ 0 & -3 & k \\\\ 0 & 6 & 42\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+2{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 10 \\\\ 0 & -3 & k \\\\ 0 & 0 & 42+2k\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the system\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+{x}_{2} &=10 \\\\ -3{x}_{2} &=k \\\\ 0 &=42+2k.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nIn order for this system to be consistent, we require $0=42+2k,$ which means that $k=-21.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186323698 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1a289e23-c521-5e54-87e0-23820eb4b3e6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321350} {:answer/id #uuid "204a0a89-e831-51e4-93db-e70840ed8600" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321388} {:answer/id #uuid "377c432d-decc-5e5a-9367-f7380ee1dac6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321568} {:answer/id #uuid "b1ae17d4-a96f-5105-94cd-190c9f5d420f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322538} {:answer/id #uuid "ea3e4ad3-76a0-55d7-9ad3-a2a4b892bc0c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322980}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321388} :answer-field/id #uuid "366ee9e6-9261-50c5-be6e-dbdc9c1112d9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323276}] :question/id #uuid "dfc6c6aa-ca5b-5544-805f-85d28c983b53" :question/math-academy-id "q-35562" :question/problem "Consider the matrix given by $A=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -7 \\\\ 1 & -4 \\\\ 3 & 5\\end{bmatrix}.$ Determine the value of $k$ for which the vector $b=\\begin{bmatrix}7 \\\\ 4 \\\\ k\\end{bmatrix}$ belongs to $\\text{Col}(A).$" :question/worked-solution "If $b$ lies in $\\text{Col}(A),$ then the equation $Ax=b$ must be consistent. So, let's find the row echelon form of the augmented matrix $[A\\,|\\,b]$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[A\\,|\\,b] & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -7 & 7 \\\\ 1 & -4 & 4 \\\\ 3 & 5 & k\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -4 & 4 \\\\ 2 & -7 & 7 \\\\ 3 & 5 & k\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -4 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 5 & k\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -4 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 17 & k-12\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-17){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -4 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & k+5\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the system\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-4{x}_{2} &=4 \\\\ {x}_{2} &=-1 \\\\ 0 &=k+5.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nIn order for this system to be consistent, we require $0=k+5,$ which means that $k=-5.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186342184 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1cb2be8f-db7e-5e30-ba66-7372af842081" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339376} {:answer/id #uuid "7c092ea3-8997-5fc9-b3ad-f38a5083d65c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340243} {:answer/id #uuid "ae4e7a0b-74ab-5b91-947d-f2d577360955" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340716} {:answer/id #uuid "da5ece3a-e3e7-50dd-8766-ef42f63657e1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341067} {:answer/id #uuid "f5eab65a-e253-5544-8b69-d25d9cb4c5be" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341301}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340243} :answer-field/id #uuid "26806f25-9816-5578-8dee-0bd821f6d86e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341447}] :question/id #uuid "51a492c4-1836-535a-a084-317ef0e2317c" :question/math-academy-id "q-74209" :question/problem "Consider the matrix given by $B=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ -2 & -3 \\\\ 5 & 7\\end{bmatrix}.$ Determine the value of $k$ for which the vector $b=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ k-3\\end{bmatrix}$ belongs to $\\text{Col}(B).$" :question/worked-solution "If $b$ lies in $\\text{Col}(B),$ then the equation $Bx=b$ must be consistent. So, let's find the row echelon form of the augmented matrix $[B\\,|\\,b]$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[B\\,|\\,b] & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ -2 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 5 & 7 & k-3\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 5 & 7 & k-3\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-5{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -3 & k+2\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+3{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & k-1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the system\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2} &=-1 \\\\ {x}_{2} &=-1 \\\\ 0 &=k-1.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nIn order for this system to be consistent, we require $0=k-1,$ which means that $k=1.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186342185 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6d91a1a7-328f-5842-9e9c-48eafec1fb37" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340097} {:answer/id #uuid "6f964c57-7228-59e8-9d64-824529a8aeda" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340118} {:answer/id #uuid "c4ca9951-003a-5b06-bba3-663b2e4ed890" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340878} {:answer/id #uuid "d38ac265-e592-5bca-a4b8-ef6fe828cad9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341001} {:answer/id #uuid "f6daedc3-62f4-5440-acc8-62ba78081fbc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341312}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340118} :answer-field/id #uuid "d8ef6738-5e99-54fc-a7a8-fdda3dcb69ca" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341763}] :question/id #uuid "035f63e6-ef7b-5c17-ba6e-584735b13fed" :question/math-academy-id "q-74212" :question/problem "Consider the matrix given by $L=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 1 \\\\ 4 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.$ Determine the value of $k$ for which the vector $b=\\begin{bmatrix}k-11 \\\\ -10 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}$ belongs to $\\text{Col}(L).$" :question/worked-solution "If $b$ lies in $\\text{Col}(L),$ then the equation $Lx=b$ must be consistent. So, let's find the row echelon form of the augmented matrix $[L\\,|\\,b]$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[L\\,|\\,b] & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 1 & k-11 \\\\ 4 & -2 & -10 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 5\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 4 & -2 & -10 \\\\ 3 & 1 & k-11\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+4{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 10 \\\\ 3 & 1 & k-11\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 10 \\\\ 0 & 4 & k+4\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-2){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 10 \\\\ 0 & 0 & k-16\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the system\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-{x}_{1}+{x}_{2} &=5 \\\\ 2{x}_{2} &=10 \\\\ 0 &=k-16.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nIn order for this system to be consistent, we require $0=k-16,$ which means that $k=16.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186342186 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0c3a91ab-7081-5091-b24c-88da6615f202" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339235} {:answer/id #uuid "6e125bd2-eb33-5d5b-a7