/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186557289 :question/id #uuid "9f8ace62-6215-5f44-93f8-e30dfc0372e6"} :step/id #uuid "dcfacae2-b140-5deb-bae8-f0b8d93c1f96" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186557337}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186557401 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186557281 :question/id #uuid "8e6e37b0-420c-5604-b7d4-9e71462bd5eb"} :step/id #uuid "de6d93f6-e851-58c8-a9b2-117e1ba0ae41"}] :activity/title "Solving Inhomogeneous Systems of ODEs Using Matrix Methods" :activity/type {:db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556414} {:activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186558671} :activity/id #uuid "10f6eef1-5078-55a6-b949-5b4bf786db94" :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186558616 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186308695 :question/id #uuid "7aef4d9e-5adf-5d9d-be87-6231a093c423"} :step/id #uuid "3cf553b5-a0c0-5e03-adcb-b5e28abcb810" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186558657}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186558657 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186558563 :question/id #uuid "cb2daa37-d9b1-570d-9a42-38ab64cc0e59"} :step/id #uuid "8b6c1363-f2b6-518d-a59c-19b0d9f1d213"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186558671 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186558544 :question/id #uuid "9a3f4d85-0623-5fd9-9cc9-8c8eac44c1ca"} :step/id #uuid "a7f36150-a323-543f-a05f-ad14ac2a2c6c" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186558616}}] :activity/title "Solving Inhomogeneous Systems of ODEs Using Matrix Methods" :activity/type {:db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186557852}] :db/id #edb/ref 17592186050707 :topic/knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186229131 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186228916 :question/id #uuid "e151cd67-cf96-5378-9380-e9960c1eb6b4" :question/math-academy-id "e-21722" :question/problem "![](images/3d/3db7e4a714d16b8f150bbca5fc9e60fdbf30da038e7dbf331dc317d6ec7c8c3c.svg)\nFill in the blanks in the expression that gives the solution of the initial value problem above.\n\n*Hint: ![](images/e7/e7b8344a953c494431f7c9594dbe6124e2e4264c3d58bc94fa383323fc85389d.svg) where ![](images/d3/d3a5e4fd69f446e59007f8e3f8c982b424deedcb837670b75c5342968b7e0549.svg)*\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\,\\,\\bbox[3pt,border:1pt solid black]{\\phantom{XXXX}}\\, \\\\ 3{e}^{4(t-1)}\\end{bmatrix}+{\\int }_{1}^{t}\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{4t} \\\\ \\,\\,\\bbox[3pt,border:1pt solid black]{\\phantom{XX}}\\,\\end{bmatrix}\\text{d}s.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Given the system $\\mathbf{x}'(t) = A \\mathbf{x}(t)+\\mathbf{g}(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, the solution of the initial value problem can be written as the sum of the homogeneous part and a particular solution:\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{x}(t) = \\underbrace{e^{A(t-t_0)} \\, \\mathbf{x}(t_0)}_{\\text{homogeneous part}} + \\underbrace{\\int_{t_0}^{t} e^{A(t-s)} \\mathbf{g}(s) \\, \\text{d}s}_{\\text{particular solution}},\n$$\n\nwhere $\\mathbf x(t_0)$ is the initial condition vector. \n\nLet's evaluate each part separately:\n\n- First, we find the homogeneous part. We are given that ![](images/7b/7b64128fdaf3565ee121779a8fcd2c84db8f639ded96f0884d6ad7e728c83b1c.svg) So,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{A(t-1)}\\,x(1) & =\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{4(t-1)} & (t-1){e}^{4(t-1)} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{4(t-1)}\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}3(t-1){e}^{4(t-1)} \\\\ 3{e}^{4(t-1)}\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Next, we find the particular solution. Notice that \n![](images/7f/7f1779e39ecb5e2bcce580d20a85eae97be505e2ad0987fa45b5b9e22c52fbbf.svg)\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s) & =\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{4(t-s)} & (t-s){e}^{4(t-s)} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{4(t-s)}\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{4s} \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{4t} \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =\\begin{bmatrix}3(t-1){e}^{4(t-1)} \\\\ 3{e}^{4(t-1)}\\end{bmatrix}+{\\int }_{1}^{t}\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{4t} \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\\text{d}s.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "95223ee8-46d8-58c2-9e3b-017adb2789e8" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186229663 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a71f00de-08de-5313-af96-a181750eb6ae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e^{2t-s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186540805}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e^{2t-s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186540805} :answer-field/id #uuid "665a164d-a4b1-5104-b010-c9d2e4fb6aae" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186228180} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ba920ad2-32c3-5075-8ddb-cb1965fbe9d9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2e^{2t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186540840}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2e^{2t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186540840} :answer-field/id #uuid "74529953-db83-50c9-b0ad-3787b4203c7b" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186228181}] :question/id #uuid "5195016b-d389-5c7b-a222-3fb5f86b99aa" :question/math-academy-id "q-334540" :question/problem "$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]x+[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{t} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nWrite down the expression that gives the solution of the initial value problem above.\n\n*Hint: ${e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{2t} & t{e}^{2t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}],$ where $A=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}].$*\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"2\">$x(t)=\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"80px\">$2t{e}^{2t}$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"2\">$\\,\\,+{\\int }_{0}^{t}\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"80px\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"2\">$\\,\\,\\text{d}s$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0$</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "Given the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+g(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, the solution of the initial value problem can be written as the sum of the homogeneous part and a particular solution:\n\n$$\nx(t)={{{e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}\\,x({t}_{0})}_{⏟}}_{\\text{homogeneous part}}+{{{\\int }_{{t}_{0}}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s}_{⏟}}_{\\text{particular solution}},\n$$\n\nwhere $x({t}_{0})$ is the initial condition vector. \n\nLet's evaluate each part separately:\n\n- First, we find the homogeneous part. We are given that ${e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{2t} & t{e}^{2t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}].$ So,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{At}\\,x(0) & =[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{2t} & t{e}^{2t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2t{e}^{2t} \\\\ 2{e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Next, we find the particular solution. Notice that \n\n$$\n{e}^{A(t-s)}=[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{2(t-s)} & (t-s){e}^{2(t-s)} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{2(t-s)}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s) & =[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{2(t-s)} & (t-s){e}^{2(t-s)} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{2(t-s)}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{e}^{s} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{2t-s} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}2t{e}^{2t} \\\\ 2{e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}]+{\\int }_{0}^{t}[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{2t-s} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\text{d}s.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186229675 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7c469a0d-2752-523c-9d5e-eb188c66277c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(5(t-1))+\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(5(t-1))" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556717} {:answer/id #uuid "e237bdb9-b23d-538d-8ede-1bde46c2390e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(5(t-1))+2\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(5(t-1))" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556988} {:answer/id #uuid "f34842c1-f721-52e9-9b77-d0abbbd36f97" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(5(t-1))-2\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(5(t-1))" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186557029}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(5(t-1))+\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(5(t-1))" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556717} :answer-field/id #uuid "c47ab649-c3da-5673-8d86-71836125878a" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186228234} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0538cbde-d100-5661-b565-1459ce5200bf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{5s}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(5(t-s))" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556439} {:answer/id #uuid "8271283e-49da-546a-bd56-2f6be5819b84" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{5s}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(5(t+s))" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556732} {:answer/id #uuid "b2307a16-a23b-5389-9b9e-da92d8558ad4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{5s}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(5(t+s))" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556867} {:answer/id #uuid "ccc40006-4513-51cc-b21e-641f0113825f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{5s}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(5(t-s))" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556924}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{5s}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(5(t-s))" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556439} :answer-field/id #uuid "48f44c01-f85c-5f3b-9309-7f51f9a7ace4" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186228238}] :question/id #uuid "5b327bcf-2ff8-5538-9740-b586ed698ad8" :question/math-academy-id "q-334922" :question/problem "$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 5 \\\\ 5 & 0\\end{aligned}]x+[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{5t} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,x(1)=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nWrite down the expression that gives the solution of the initial value problem above.\n\n*Hint: ${e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(5t) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(5t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(5t) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(5t)\\end{aligned}],$ where $A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 5 \\\\ 5 & 0\\end{aligned}].$*\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"2\">$x(t)=\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"160px\">$2\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(5(t-1))+\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(5(t-1))$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td><td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"2\">$\\,\\,+{\\int }_{1}^{t}\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"160px\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"2\">$\\,\\,\\text{d}s$</td>\n</tr><tr>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td><td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">${e}^{5s}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(5(t-s))$</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "Given the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+g(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, the solution of the initial value problem can be written as the sum of the homogeneous part and a particular solution:\n\n$$\nx(t)={{{e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}\\,x({t}_{0})}_{⏟}}_{\\text{homogeneous part}}+{{{\\int }_{{t}_{0}}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s}_{⏟}}_{\\text{particular solution}},\n$$\n\nwhere $x({t}_{0})$ is the initial condition vector. \n\nLet's evaluate each part separately:\n\n- First, we find the homogeneous part. We are given that ${e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(5t) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(5t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(5t) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(5t)\\end{aligned}].$ So,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{A(t-1)}\\,x(1) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(5(t-1)) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(5(t-1)) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(5(t-1)) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(5(t-1))\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(5(t-1))+\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(5(t-1)) \\\\ 2\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(5(t-1))+\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(5(t-1))\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Next, we find the particular solution. Notice that \n\n$$\n{e}^{A(t-s)}=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(5(t-s)) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(5(t-s)) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(5(t-s)) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(5(t-s))\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(5(t-s)) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(5(t-s)) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(5(t-s)) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(5(t-s))\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{e}^{5s} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{5s}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(5(t-s)) \\\\ {e}^{5s}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(5(t-s))\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(5(t-1))+\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(5(t-1)) \\\\ 2\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(5(t-1))+\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(5(t-1))\\end{aligned}]+{\\int }_{1}^{t}[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{5s}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(5(t-s)) \\\\ {e}^{5s}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(5(t-s))\\end{aligned}]\\text{d}s.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186308688 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7d4bfced-4c23-541f-b242-4c2ea02d35eb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{3t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306347} {:answer/id #uuid "72e16707-4ff3-5dfd-9eed-366cbfa6fe18" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e^{3t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186479531}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e^{3t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186479531} :answer-field/id #uuid "52d98b8a-0ce9-5cfa-a498-ed17c16b2e6d" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307772} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f1c22720-1aa8-597e-9b76-8432cec4de4e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{3t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307375} {:answer/id #uuid "27dc7621-01eb-5ac6-8247-fe730465d634" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e^{3t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186479418}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e^{3t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186479418} :answer-field/id #uuid "cba95706-4eaf-526e-986f-73babc57c464" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308154}] :question/id #uuid "001f1d7b-e465-5a31-aa71-fce5efbdd939" :question/math-academy-id "q-334824" :question/problem "$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{bmatrix}x+\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ {e}^{3t}\\end{bmatrix},\\,x(0)=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nWrite down the expression that gives the solution of the initial value problem above.\n\n*Hint: ${e}^{At}=\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{3t} & t{e}^{3t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{3t}\\end{bmatrix},$ where $A=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{bmatrix}.$*\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"2\">$x(t)=\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"80px\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"2\">$\\,\\,+{\\int }_{0}^{t}\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"80px\">$(t-s){e}^{3t}$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"2\">$\\,\\,\\text{d}s$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0$</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "Given the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+g(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, the solution of the initial value problem can be written as the sum of the homogeneous part and a particular solution:\n\n$$\nx(t)={{{e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}\\,x({t}_{0})}_{⏟}}_{\\text{homogeneous part}}+{{{\\int }_{{t}_{0}}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s}_{⏟}}_{\\text{particular solution}},\n$$\n\nwhere $x({t}_{0})$ is the initial condition vector. \n\nLet's evaluate each part separately:\n\n- First, we find the homogeneous part. We are given that ${e}^{At}=\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{3t} & t{e}^{3t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{3t}\\end{bmatrix}.$ So,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{At}\\,x(0) & =\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{3t} & t{e}^{3t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{3t}\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{3t} \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Next, we find the particular solution. Notice that \n\n$$\n{e}^{A(t-s)}=\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{3(t-s)} & (t-s){e}^{3(t-s)} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{3(t-s)}\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s) & =\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{3(t-s)} & (t-s){e}^{3(t-s)} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{3(t-s)}\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ {e}^{3s}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}(t-s){e}^{3t} \\\\ {e}^{3t}\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{3t} \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+{\\int }_{0}^{t}\\begin{bmatrix}(t-s){e}^{3t} \\\\ {e}^{3t}\\end{bmatrix}\\text{d}s.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186308692 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "237ca5ab-34cd-58e7-9713-b55a6e87c11b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{5t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305489}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{5t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305489} :answer-field/id #uuid "1dd60399-b452-5b9e-ab6f-1b2c49d47ce4" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307619} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "752cf0f7-34a2-5108-a051-4523e28c9195" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{e}^{5(t-1)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306265}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{e}^{5(t-1)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306265} :answer-field/id #uuid "92d548ec-0d73-5a36-8fa4-84091d6ec494" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307985}] :question/id #uuid "cc8319e7-c74a-546c-ac46-138a893fec53" :question/math-academy-id "q-334848" :question/problem "$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 5\\end{bmatrix}x+\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{5t} \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,x(1)=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nWrite down the expression that gives the solution of the initial value problem above.\n\n*Hint: ${e}^{At}=\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{5t} & t{e}^{5t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{5t}\\end{bmatrix},$ where $A=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 5\\end{bmatrix}.$*\n\n| $x(t)=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} |  | $\\,\\,+{\\int }_{1}^{t}\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-2}} |  | $\\,\\,\\text{d}s$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $0$ |  |  | $0$ |  |  |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "Given the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+g(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, the solution of the initial value problem can be written as the sum of the homogeneous part and a particular solution:\n\n$$\nx(t)={{{e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}\\,x({t}_{0})}_{⏟}}_{\\text{homogeneous part}}+{{{\\int }_{{t}_{0}}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s}_{⏟}}_{\\text{particular solution}},\n$$\n\nwhere $x({t}_{0})$ is the initial condition vector. \n\nLet's evaluate each part separately:\n\n- First, we find the homogeneous part. We are given that ${e}^{At}=\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{5t} & t{e}^{5t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{5t}\\end{bmatrix}.$ So,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{A(t-1)}\\,x(1) & =\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{5(t-1)} & (t-1){e}^{5(t-1)} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{5(t-1)}\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}2{e}^{5(t-1)} \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Next, we find the particular solution. Notice that \n\n$$\n{e}^{A(t-s)}=\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{5(t-s)} & (t-s){e}^{5(t-s)} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{5(t-s)}\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s) & =\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{5(t-s)} & (t-s){e}^{5(t-s)} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{5(t-s)}\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{5s} \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{5t} \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =\\begin{bmatrix}2{e}^{5(t-1)} \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+{\\int }_{1}^{t}\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{5t} \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\\text{d}s.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186308695 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "160b514e-c7a9-5db1-8962-33d86d078fb4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}(2(t-s))" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305342}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}(2(t-s))" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305342} :answer-field/id #uuid "63437be9-2066-5dad-a01a-a0e02722c169" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307836} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "05184db4-a95b-5878-863f-1aa2b4e40630" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\operatorname{cos}(2t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305198}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\operatorname{cos}(2t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305198} :answer-field/id #uuid "f1530c65-7d45-5311-814a-529b693ace24" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308286}] :question/id #uuid "7aef4d9e-5adf-5d9d-be87-6231a093c423" :question/math-academy-id "q-334855" :question/problem "$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 0\\end{bmatrix}x+\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,x(0)=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nWrite down the expression that gives the solution of the initial value problem above.\n\n*Hint: ${e}^{At}=\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t) & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)\\end{bmatrix},$ where $A=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.$*\n\n| $x(t)=\\,\\,$ |  | $3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)$ |  | $\\,\\,+{\\int }_{0}^{t}\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} |  | $\\,\\,\\text{d}s$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-2}} |  |  | $-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2(t-s))$ |  |  |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "Given the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+g(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, the solution of the initial value problem can be written as the sum of the homogeneous part and a particular solution:\n\n$$\nx(t)={{{e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}\\,x({t}_{0})}_{⏟}}_{\\text{homogeneous part}}+{{{\\int }_{{t}_{0}}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s}_{⏟}}_{\\text{particular solution}},\n$$\n\nwhere $x({t}_{0})$ is the initial condition vector. \n\nLet's evaluate each part separately:\n\n- First, we find the homogeneous part. We are given that ${e}^{At}=\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t) & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)\\end{bmatrix}.$ So,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{At}\\,x(0) & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t) & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t) \\\\ 3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Next, we find the particular solution. Notice that \n\n$$\n{e}^{A(t-s)}=\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2(t-s)) & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2(t-s)) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2(t-s)) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(2(t-s))\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s) & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2(t-s)) & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2(t-s)) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2(t-s)) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(2(t-s))\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2(t-s)) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2(t-s))\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =\\begin{bmatrix}3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t) \\\\ 3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)\\end{bmatrix}+{\\int }_{0}^{t}\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2(t-s)) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2(t-s))\\end{bmatrix}\\text{d}s.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186308696 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b12c1e03-c805-5e36-aea2-b6d121e73478" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}(4(t-s))" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306815} {:answer/id #uuid "74474233-2fa8-51ba-9cb4-da5296695f41" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\cos(4(t-s))" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186479536}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\cos(4(t-s))" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186479536} :answer-field/id #uuid "13f5abdf-75a7-5b21-afa3-653d497c5d41" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307584} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ab25cf3f-5e10-5e03-b9ec-f