align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "Given the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+g(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, the solution of the initial value problem can be written as the sum of the homogeneous part and a particular solution:\n\n$$\nx(t)={{{e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}\\,x({t}_{0})}_{⏟}}_{\\text{homogeneous part}}+{{{\\int }_{{t}_{0}}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s}_{⏟}}_{\\text{particular solution}},\n$$\n\nwhere $x({t}_{0})$ is the initial condition vector. \n\nLet's evaluate each part separately:\n\n- First, we find the homogeneous part. We are given that ${e}^{At}=\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t) & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t)\\end{bmatrix}.$ So,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{At}\\,x(0) & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t) & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t)\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}5\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t) \\\\ 5\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t)\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Next, we find the particular solution. Notice that \n\n$$\n{e}^{A(t-s)}=\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4(t-s)) & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(4(t-s)) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4(t-s)) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(4(t-s))\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s) & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4(t-s)) & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(4(t-s)) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4(t-s)) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(4(t-s))\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4(t-s)) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4(t-s))\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =\\begin{bmatrix}5\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t) \\\\ 5\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t)\\end{bmatrix}+{\\int }_{0}^{t}\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4(t-s)) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4(t-s))\\end{bmatrix}\\text{d}s.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186370149 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "19c56caf-0eb5-54a8-9d9d-bc69ddd10352" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3{e}^{2(t-1)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370151}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3{e}^{2(t-1)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370151} :answer-field/id #uuid "087bba7d-d3a8-5620-b937-c6594cac637f" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370150} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4570a24e-2d22-5ba8-ac78-caaadd9407fe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{2t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370153}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{2t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370153} :answer-field/id #uuid "06c3666e-af27-5e99-9047-9da96e1fb451" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370152}] :question/id #uuid "20a2d840-1833-5432-8cfc-283ba2fd018f" :question/math-academy-id "q-334830" :question/problem "$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}x+\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{2t} \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,x(1)=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nWrite down the expression that gives the solution of the initial value problem above.\n\n*Hint: ${e}^{At}=\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{2t} & t{e}^{2t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{2t}\\end{bmatrix},$ where $A=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}.$*\n\n| $x(t)=\\,\\,$ |  | $3(t-1){e}^{2(t-1)}$ |  | $\\,\\,+{\\int }_{1}^{t}\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} |  | $\\,\\,\\text{d}s$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-2}} |  |  | $0$ |  |  |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "Given the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+g(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, the solution of the initial value problem can be written as the sum of the homogeneous part and a particular solution:\n\n$$\nx(t)={{{e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}\\,x({t}_{0})}_{⏟}}_{\\text{homogeneous part}}+{{{\\int }_{{t}_{0}}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s}_{⏟}}_{\\text{particular solution}},\n$$\n\nwhere $x({t}_{0})$ is the initial condition vector. \n\nLet's evaluate each part separately:\n\n- First, we find the homogeneous part. We are given that ${e}^{At}=\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{2t} & t{e}^{2t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{2t}\\end{bmatrix}.$ So,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{A(t-1)}\\,x(1) & =\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{2(t-1)} & (t-1){e}^{2(t-1)} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{2(t-1)}\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}3(t-1){e}^{2(t-1)} \\\\ 3{e}^{2(t-1)}\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Next, we find the particular solution. Notice that \n\n$$\n{e}^{A(t-s)}=\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{2(t-s)} & (t-s){e}^{2(t-s)} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{2(t-s)}\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s) & =\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{2(t-s)} & (t-s){e}^{2(t-s)} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{2(t-s)}\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{2s} \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{2t} \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =\\begin{bmatrix}3(t-1){e}^{2(t-1)} \\\\ 3{e}^{2(t-1)}\\end{bmatrix}+{\\int }_{1}^{t}\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{2t} \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\\text{d}s.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186396516 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "724c6608-ba55-593a-b831-9342a1ad2fe4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{2s}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2(t-s))" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396518} {:answer/id #uuid "6d012455-60c7-55cd-8abe-a5ae87c14843" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{2s}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2(t-s))" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396519} {:answer/id #uuid "f37ded06-8f51-502f-9066-f2e3021a9d5c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{2s}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2(t+s))" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396520} {:answer/id #uuid "61927b3b-fbb4-54e5-bcfd-ea2b2a