the solution of the initial value problem above.\n\n*Hint: ${e}^{At}=\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2t) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2t) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2t)\\end{bmatrix},$ where $A=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.$*\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"2\">$x(t)=\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"170px\">$3\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2(t-1))+\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2(t-1))$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td><td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"2\">$\\,\\,+{\\int }_{1}^{t}\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"170px\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"2\">$\\,\\,\\text{d}s$</td>\n</tr><tr>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td><td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">${e}^{2s}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2(t-s))$</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "Given the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+g(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, the solution of the initial value problem can be written as the sum of the homogeneous part and a particular solution:\n\n$$\nx(t)={{{e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}\\,x({t}_{0})}_{⏟}}_{\\text{homogeneous part}}+{{{\\int }_{{t}_{0}}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s}_{⏟}}_{\\text{particular solution}},\n$$\n\nwhere $x({t}_{0})$ is the initial condition vector. \n\nLet's evaluate each part separately:\n\n- First, we find the homogeneous part. We are given that ${e}^{At}=\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2t) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2t) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2t)\\end{bmatrix}.$ So,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{A(t-1)}\\,x(1) & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2(t-1)) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2(t-1)) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2(t-1)) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2(t-1))\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}3\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2(t-1))+\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2(t-1)) \\\\ 3\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2(t-1))+\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2(t-1))\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Next, we find the particular solution. Notice that \n\n$$\n{e}^{A(t-s)}=\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2(t-s)) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2(t-s)) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2(t-s)) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2(t-s))\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s) & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2(t-s)) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2(t-s)) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2(t-s)) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2(t-s))\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{2s} \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{2s}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2(t-s)) \\\\ {e}^{2s}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2(t-s))\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =\\begin{bmatrix}3\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2(t-1))+\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2(t-1)) \\\\ 3\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2(t-1))+\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2(t-1))\\end{bmatrix}+{\\int }_{1}^{t}\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{2s}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2(t-s)) \\\\ {e}^{2s}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2(t-s))\\end{bmatrix}\\text{d}s.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186479848 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1469716d-c345-5ffe-8890-e1981e80d56a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(4t)+\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(4t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186479390} {:answer/id #uuid "3a5c4e43-e417-5c07-a2c3-eb9628d96e3b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(4t)-3\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(4t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186479445} {:answer/id #uuid "740b8e1d-0233-597c-ac41-6431abd888f5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(4t)+3\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(4t)" :db/id