itial value problem above.\n\n*Hint: ${e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(6t) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(6t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(6t) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(6t)\\end{aligned}],$ where $A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 6 \\\\ 6 & 0\\end{aligned}].$*\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"2\">$x(t)=\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"180px\">$2\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(6(t-1))+\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(6(t-1))$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td><td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"2\">$\\,\\,+{\\int }_{1}^{t}\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"180px\">${e}^{6s}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(6(t-s))$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"2\">$\\,\\,\\text{d}s$</td>\n</tr><tr>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td><td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "Given the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+g(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, the solution of the initial value problem can be written as the sum of the homogeneous part and a particular solution:\n\n$$\nx(t)={{{e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}\\,x({t}_{0})}_{⏟}}_{\\text{homogeneous part}}+{{{\\int }_{{t}_{0}}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s}_{⏟}}_{\\text{particular solution}},\n$$\n\nwhere $x({t}_{0})$ is the initial condition vector. \n\nLet's evaluate each part separately:\n\n- First, we find the homogeneous part. We are given that ${e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(6t) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(6t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(6t) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(6t)\\end{aligned}].$ So,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{A(t-1)}\\,x(1) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(6(t-1)) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(6(t-1)) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(6(t-1)) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(6(t-1))\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(6(t-1))+\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(6(t-1)) \\\\ 2\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(6(t-1))+\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(6(t-1))\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Next, we find the particular solution. Notice that \n\n$$\n{e}^{A(t-s)}=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(6(t-s)) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(6(t-s)) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(6(t-s)) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(6(t-s))\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(6(t-s)) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(6(t-s)) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(6(t-s)) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(6(t-s))\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ {e}^{6s}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{6s}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(6(t-s)) \\\\ {e}^{6s}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(6(t-s))\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(6(t-1))+\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(6(t-1)) \\\\ 2\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(6(t-1))+\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(6(t-1))\\end{aligned}]+{\\int }_{1}^{t}[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{6s}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(6(t-s)) \\\\ {e}^{6s}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(6(t-s))\\end{aligned}]\\text{d}s.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186557289 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "646e6165-7c3a-5090-b755-0054dbd03146" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "te^{4t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556660}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "te^{4t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556660} :answer-field/id #uuid "174e2ccc-42c8-5609-b37a-59d23929885c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186557078} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "aca58c0a-4a82-5bea-94ab-b3068980a554" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e^{4t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556855}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e^{4t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556855} :answer-field/id #uuid "5604af13-50f7-5867-8a20-353ebbce0164" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186557114}] :question/id #uuid "9f8ace62-6215-5f44-93f8-e30dfc0372e6" :question/math-academy-id "q-334828" :question/problem "$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{aligned}]x+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ {e}^{4t}\\end{aligned}],\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nWrite down the expression that gives the solution of the initial value problem above.\n\n*Hint: ${e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{4t} & t{e}^{4t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{4t}\\end{aligned}],$ where $A=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{aligned}].$*\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"2\">$x(t)=\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"80px\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"2\">$\\,\\,+{\\int }_{0}^{t}\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"80px\">$(t-s){e}^{4t}$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"2\">$\\,\\,\\text{d}s$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">${e}^{4t}$</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "Given the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+g(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, the solution of the initial value problem can be written as the sum of the homogeneous part and a particular solution:\n\n$$\nx(t)={{{e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}\\,x({t}_{0})}_{⏟}}_{\\text{homogeneous part}}+{{{\\int }_{{t}_{0}}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s}_{⏟}}_{\\text{particular solution}},\n$$\n\nwhere $x({t}_{0})$ is the initial condition vector. \n\nLet's evaluate each part separately:\n\n- First, we find the homogeneous part. We are given that ${e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{4t} & t{e}^{4t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{4t}\\end{aligned}].$ So,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{At}\\,x(0) & =[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{4t} & t{e}^{4t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{4t}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}t{e}^{4t} \\\\ {e}^{4t}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Next, we find the particular solution. Notice that \n\n$$\n{e}^{A(t-s)}=[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{4(t-s)} & (t-s){e}^{4(t-s)} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{4(t-s)}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s) & =[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{4(t-s)} & (t-s){e}^{4(t-s)} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{4(t-s)}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ {e}^{4s}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}(t-s){e}^{4t} \\\\ {e}^{4t}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}t{e}^{4t} \\\\ {e}^{4t}\\end{aligned}]+{\\int }_{0}^{t}[\\begin{aligned}(t-s){e}^{4t} \\\\ {e}^{4t}\\end{aligned}]\\text{d}s.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186557325 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b5b356a7-3b0b-5f1f-bec8-e6b826f26b86" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\cos t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556876}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\cos t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556876} :answer-field/id #uuid "17254fb8-737c-5411-ba14-63458b8c5c1e" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186557077} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c887629a-5ab0-5f5a-85b8-798e29da3914" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\cos(t-s)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556912}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\cos(t-s)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556912} :answer-field/id #uuid "adcf2066-3be2-5f5c-966d-7fbfbab80820" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186557162}] :question/id #uuid "f491a1e5-e94d-5b1b-9331-94aa4176665c" :question/math-academy-id "q-334856" :question/problem "$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}]x+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nWrite down the expression that gives the solution of the initial value problem above.\n\n*Hint: ${e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t & \\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡t & \\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\end{aligned}],$ where $A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}].$*\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"2\">$x(t)=\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"80px\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"2\">$\\,\\,+{\\int }_{0}^{t}\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"80px\">$\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t-s)$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"2\">$\\,\\,\\text{d}s$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">$-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t$</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "Given the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+g(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, the solution of the initial value problem can be written as the sum of the homogeneous part and a particular solution:\n\n$$\nx(t)={{{e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}\\,x({t}_{0})}_{⏟}}_{\\text{homogeneous part}}+{{{\\int }_{{t}_{0}}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s}_{⏟}}_{\\text{particular solution}},\n$$\n\nwhere $x({t}_{0})$ is the initial condition vector. \n\nLet's evaluate each part separately:\n\n- First, we find the homogeneous part. We are given that ${e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t & \\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡t & \\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\end{aligned}].$ So,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{At}\\,x(0) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t & \\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡t & \\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\ -2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Next, we find the particular solution. Notice that \n\n$$\n{e}^{A(t-s)}=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t-s) & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(t-s) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t-s) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(t-s)\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t-s) & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(t-s) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t-s) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(t-s)\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t-s) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(t-s)\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\ -2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{aligned}]+{\\int }_{0}^{t}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t-s) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(t-s)\\end{aligned}]\\text{d}s.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186558544 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d59687fe-7fee-536b-ae53-62aa4e2062c6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e^{3t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558287}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e^{3t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558287} :answer-field/id #uuid "bda1e7e4-3c88-5a06-909e-308c1b22da65" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558451} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "81eb1113-b696-53f5-ab1f-005ae9690189" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e^{3(t-1)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558118}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e^{3(t-1)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558118} :answer-field/id #uuid "fc834a44-d315-5323-8d37-5104d3268aa9" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558476}] :question/id #uuid "9a3f4d85-0623-5fd9-9cc9-8c8eac44c1ca" :question/math-academy-id "q-334846" :question/problem "$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}]x+[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{3t} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,x(1)=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nWrite down the expression that gives the solution of the initial value problem above.\n\n*Hint: ${e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{3t} & t{e}^{3t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{3t}\\end{aligned}],$ where $A=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}].$*\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"2\">$x(t)=\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"80px\">$(t-2){e}^{3(t-1)}$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"2\">$\\,\\,+{\\int }_{1}^{t}\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"80px\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"2\">$\\,\\,\\text{d}s$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0$</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "Given the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+g(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, the solution of the initial value problem can be written as the sum of the homogeneous part and a particular solution:\n\n$$\nx(t)={{{e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}\\,x({t}_{0})}_{⏟}}_{\\text{homogeneous part}}+{{{\\int }_{{t}_{0}}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s}_{⏟}}_{\\text{particular solution}},\n$$\n\nwhere $x({t}_{0})$ is the initial condition vector. \n\nLet's evaluate each part separately:\n\n- First, we find the homogeneous part. We are given that ${e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{3t} & t{e}^{3t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{3t}\\end{aligned}].$ So,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{A(t-1)}\\,x(1) & =[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{3(t-1)} & (t-1){e}^{3(t-1)} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{3(t-1)}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}(t-2){e}^{3(t-1)} \\\\ {e}^{3(t-1)}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Next, we find the particular solution. Notice that \n\n$$\n{e}^{A(t-s)}=[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{3(t-s)} & (t-s){e}^{3(t-s)} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{3(t-s)}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s) & =[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{3(t-s)} & (t-s){e}^{3(t-s)} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{3(t-s)}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{e}^{3s} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{3t} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}(t-2){e}^{3(t-1)} \\\\ {e}^{3(t-1)}\\end{aligned}]+{\\int }_{1}^{t}[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{3t} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\text{d}s.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186558563 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "325e2bea-79c6-5d0e-86e5-ca3c08841f5a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{s}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(t+s)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186557971} {:answer/id #uuid "8e624ff8-2ee1-5b70-ba81-5895a41c4248" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{s}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(t-s)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558145} {:answer/id #uuid "b4ecf254-834a-5dbe-8b2d-44e08553fb02" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{s}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(t-s)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558228} {:answer/id #uuid "f6893209-e8c4-5a46-9f8a-822f69bcdaf7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{s}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(t+s)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558350}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{s}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(t-s)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558228} :answer-field/id #uuid "dadfc882-5148-5c0c-af21-a9e418a22bd6" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558464} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "69fe7ba5-1b53-56bf-9a9f-f5c568562239" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(t)+2\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558069} {:answer/id #uuid "8c6829ae-e7c1-5884-afa0-116dfe94231c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(t)+\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558142} {:answer/id #uuid "ad7f1da6-be8e-55ae-86e2-b2f30e2b8500" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(t)-2\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558212} {:answer/id #uuid "c87fcfa6-f6e3-5441-b2a1-174c935027eb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(t)+2\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558267}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(t)+2\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558069} :answer-field/id #uuid "ffb55f3c-2681-5734-9a74-f7bf06c53fcc" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558478}] :question/id #uuid "cb2daa37-d9b1-570d-9a42-38ab64cc0e59" :question/math-academy-id "q-334859" :question/problem "$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]x+[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{t} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nWrite down the expression that gives the solution of the initial value problem above.\n\n*Hint: ${e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(t) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(t) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(t)\\end{aligned}],$ where $A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}].$*\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"2\">$x(t)=\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"120px\">$\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(t)+2\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(t)$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td><td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"2\">$\\,\\,+{\\int }_{0}^{t}\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"120px\">{{field-1}} </td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"2\">$\\,\\,\\text{d}s$</td>\n</tr><tr>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td><td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">${e}^{s}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(t-s)$</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "Given the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+g(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, the solution of the initial value problem can be written as the sum of the homogeneous part and a particular solution:\n\n$$\nx(t)={{{e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}\\,x({t}_{0})}_{⏟}}_{\\text{homogeneous part}}+{{{\\int }_{{t}_{0}}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s}_{⏟}}_{\\text{particular solution}},\n$$\n\nwhere $x({t}_{0})$ is the initial condition vector. \n\nLet's evaluate each part separately:\n\n- First, we find the homogeneous part. We are given that ${e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(t) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(t) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(t)\\end{aligned}].$ So,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{At}\\,x(0) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(t) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(t) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(t)\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(t)+2\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(t)+2\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(t)\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Next, we find the particular solution. Notice that \n\n$$\n{e}^{A(t-s)}=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(t-s) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(t-s) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(t-s) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(t-s)\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(t-s) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(t-s) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(t-s) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(t-s)\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{e}^{s} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{s}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(t-s) \\\\ {e}^{s}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(t-s)\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(t)+2\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(t)+2\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(t)\\end{aligned}]+{\\int }_{0}^{t}[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{s}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(t-s) \\\\ {e}^{s}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(t-s)\\end{aligned}]\\text{d}s.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Matrix Exponential Formula for IVP Solution of an Inhomogeneous System"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186229132 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186228914 :question/id #uuid "3638fd11-5f61-5656-89c4-18ee0a4318ac" :question/math-academy-id "e-21720" :question/problem "![](images/b2/b295374b3b08a5d81309c92f39b38e29f1e44159a8c96e7fdfeb4cc561818585.svg)\nFind the solution to the initial value problem above.\n\n*Hint: ![](images/e7/e773bbc2fc731a397cc747fffa2e5424a30a513e8b56e0337c56bbbe7953f837.svg) where ![](images/9b/9b205047979771af4c5e88a6a9798729cb464fa080b0b46cbfc70b3c77ce8a83.svg)*" :question/worked-solution "Writing our system in matrix form, we get\n![](images/80/8004eea851883dbf0360ca3e5f39678967cdf5060668508f65cf3e5d54d6b027.svg)\nwhere ![](images/eb/ebe84b2cfbe7f95afe2c819b1d1d7790061c81744295076ac5bc739c13832dbe.svg) and ![](images/ed/edd1f7c4e50501b6849b37c98e822621d64d2f5d90a5de35b96d569814bb2a3a.svg) So, the matrix of the system is ![](images/5c/5c91edafde3ff3c119a58783296b9f8c56ecd3604d6b663af6d764a911fe1d72.svg)\n\nGiven the system $\\mathbf{x}'(t) = A \\mathbf{x}(t)+\\mathbf{g}(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, the solution of the initial value problem can be written as the sum of the homogeneous part and a particular solution:\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{x}(t) = \\underbrace{e^{A(t-t_0)} \\, \\mathbf{x}(t_0)}_{\\text{homogeneous part}} + \\underbrace{\\int_{t_0}^{t} e^{A(t-s)} \\mathbf{g}(s) \\, \\text{d}s}_{\\text{particular solution}},\n$$\n\nwhere $\\mathbf x(t_0)$ is the initial condition vector. \n\nLet's evaluate each part separately:\n\n- First, we find the homogeneous part. We are given that \n![](images/ed/ed77716162d9ecdeee50cd26172985ed4a5038cad903ca4729da1d9895fc9cc4.svg)\nSince the initial conditions are given at $t = t_0 = 0,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}x(0) & ={e}^{At}\\,x(0) \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{3t} & t{e}^{3t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{3t}\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Next, we find the particular solution. Notice that \n![](images/22/22f92a117def6f3377a72f871d58d23cf339290a55c0f7d297ccb797b5046bf7.svg)\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s) & =\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{3(t-s)} & (t-s){e}^{3(t-s)} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{3(t-s)}\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{3(t-s)} \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{-3s+3t} \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{0}^{t}\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{-3s+3t} \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\\text{d}s \\\\  & ={\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{1}{3}{e}^{-3s+3t} \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}}_{s=0}^{s=t} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{3}{e}^{3t}-\\frac{1}{3} \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{3}{e}^{3t}-\\frac{1}{3} \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{3}{e}^{3t}-\\frac{1}{3} \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{3t}-1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n![](images/34/348882682fbf17c25c759980898770a40422158cc3592d1fa51aa73a941f5cb6.svg)"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4eca32dd-1563-55c6-b594-08588efd601b" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186229661 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a299d73d-b583-53ef-be26-b86c2a86c4fe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1-3\\operatorname{cos}(2t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306680} {:answer/id #uuid "ba6921c8-3a4c-5512-a27f-32ceedf7733d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1-3\\cos(2t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186479638}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1-3\\cos(2t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186479638} :answer-field/id #uuid "34d2e73a-19d2-55b4-928e-3eac2de41f20" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307686}] :question/id #uuid "6f94a953-d6ae-5d71-b1d5-f509cb5bc306" :question/math-academy-id "q-334531" :question/problem "$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t) &=2y(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t) &=-2x(t)+1,\\end{aligned}\\right.\\,\\begin{bmatrix}x(0) \\\\ y(0)\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the initial value problem above.\n\n*Hint: ${e}^{At}=\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t) & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)\\end{bmatrix},$ where $A=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.$*\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"2\">$\\begin{bmatrix}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{bmatrix}=\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"120px\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">$3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)$</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "Writing our system in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 0\\end{bmatrix}x(t)+g(t),\n$$\n\nwhere $x(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{bmatrix}$ and $g(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}.$ So, the matrix of the system is $A=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\nGiven the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+g(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, the solution of the initial value problem can be written as the sum of the homogeneous part and a particular solution:\n\n$$\nx(t)={{{e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}\\,x({t}_{0})}_{⏟}}_{\\text{homogeneous part}}+{{{\\int }_{{t}_{0}}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s}_{⏟}}_{\\text{particular solution}},\n$$\n\nwhere $x({t}_{0})$ is the initial condition vector. \n\nLet's evaluate each part separately:\n\n- First, we find the homogeneous part. We are given that \n\n$$\n{e}^{At}=\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t) & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nSince the initial conditions are given at $t={t}_{0}=0,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})} & ={e}^{At}\\,x(0) \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t) & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Next, we find the particular solution. Notice that \n\n$$\n{e}^{A(t-s)}=\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2(t-s)) & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2(t-s)) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2(t-s)) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(2(t-s))\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s) & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2(t-s)) & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2(t-s)) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2(t-s)) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(2(t-s))\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2(t-s)) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(2(t-s))\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{0}^{t}\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2(t-s)) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(2(t-s))\\end{bmatrix}\\text{d}s \\\\  & ={\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2(t-s)) \\\\ -\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2(t-s))\\end{bmatrix}}_{s=0}^{s=t} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =\\begin{bmatrix}-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)\\end{bmatrix}+\\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}1-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t) \\\\ 3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186229678 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "01b710ba-ff00-564b-aa56-a218823c5a34" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(3t)+1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370308} {:answer/id #uuid "115a425c-7d5a-5e6a-a6a9-f0d774f944ae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(3t)-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370309} {:answer/id #uuid "039d6594-16e9-5ee1-a93f-756747ec02c2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(3t)-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370310} {:answer/id #uuid "e2c3a851-f331-52ed-aa7f-b2a15aaca90c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(3t)+1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370311}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(3t)-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370310} :answer-field/id #uuid "04307a93-eb46-548d-9a4a-4bf90a0e6697" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370307}] :question/id #uuid "b9fcadd6-0c1a-598a-b135-72da1abeb4f3" :question/math-academy-id "q-335088" :question/problem "$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t) &=3y(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t) &=3x(t)+3,\\end{aligned}\\right.\\,\\begin{bmatrix}x(0) \\\\ y(0)\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the initial value problem above.\n\n*Hint: ${e}^{At}=\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(3t) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(3t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(3t) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(3t)\\end{bmatrix},$ where $A=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.$*\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"2\">$\\begin{bmatrix}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{bmatrix}=\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"80px\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n</tr><tr>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">$\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(3t)$</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "Writing our system in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 0\\end{bmatrix}x(t)+g(t),\n$$\n\nwhere $x(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{bmatrix}$ and $g(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}.$ So, the matrix of the system is $A=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\nGiven the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+g(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, the solution of the initial value problem can be written as the sum of the homogeneous part and a particular solution:\n\n$$\nx(t)={{{e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}\\,x({t}_{0})}_{⏟}}_{\\text{homogeneous part}}+{{{\\int }_{{t}_{0}}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s}_{⏟}}_{\\text{particular solution}},\n$$\n\nwhere $x({t}_{0})$ is the initial condition vector. \n\nLet's evaluate each part separately:\n\n- First, we find the homogeneous part. We are given that \n\n$$\n{e}^{At}=\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(3t) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(3t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(3t) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(3t)\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nSince the initial conditions are given at $t={t}_{0}=0,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})} & ={e}^{At}\\,x(0) \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(3t) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(3t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(3t) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(3t)\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Next, we find the particular solution. Notice that \n\n$$\n{e}^{A(t-s)}=\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(3(t-s)) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(3(t-s)) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(3(t-s)) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(3(t-s))\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s) & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(3(t-s)) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(3(t-s)) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(3(t-s)) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(3(t-s))\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}3\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(3(t-s)) \\\\ 3\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(3(t-s))\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{0}^{t}\\begin{bmatrix}3\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(3(t-s)) \\\\ 3\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(3(t-s))\\end{bmatrix}\\text{d}s \\\\  & ={\\begin{bmatrix}-\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(3(t-s)) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(3(t-s))\\end{bmatrix}}_{s=0}^{s=t} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(3t)-1 \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(3t)\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(3t)-1 \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(3t)\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(3t)-1 \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(3t)\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186308718 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c139fc5d-402e-5c97-b048-caf60e14b36c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{sin}(2t)-\\operatorname{cos}(2t)+3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306955} {:answer/id #uuid "6963f53e-90b3-59a4-b3ac-6bc885da9965" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3-\\cos(2t)+2\\sin(2t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494533}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3-\\cos(2t)+2\\sin(2t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494533} :answer-field/id #uuid "8b933995-aeb2-5960-92c8-2edb1a0843a3" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307958}] :question/id #uuid "03656a1f-f3fa-5cdf-b35f-3b5febfaad49" :question/math-academy-id "q-335054" :question/problem "$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t) &=2y(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t) &=-2x(t)+3,\\end{aligned}\\right.\\,\\begin{bmatrix}x(0) \\\\ y(0)\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the initial value problem above.\n\n*Hint: ${e}^{At}=\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t) & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)\\end{bmatrix},$ where $A=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.$*\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"2\">$\\begin{bmatrix}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{bmatrix}=\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"180px\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">$\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)$</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "Writing our system in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 0\\end{bmatrix}x(t)+g(t),\n$$\n\nwhere $x(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{bmatrix}$ and $g(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}.$ So, the matrix of the system is $A=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\nGiven the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+g(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, the solution of the initial value problem can be written as the sum of the homogeneous part and a particular solution:\n\n$$\nx(t)={{{e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}\\,x({t}_{0})}_{⏟}}_{\\text{homogeneous part}}+{{{\\int }_{{t}_{0}}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s}_{⏟}}_{\\text{particular solution}},\n$$\n\nwhere $x({t}_{0})$ is the initial condition vector. \n\nLet's evaluate each part separately:\n\n- First, we find the homogeneous part. We are given that \n\n$$\n{e}^{At}=\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t) & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nSince the initial conditions are given at $t={t}_{0}=0,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})} & ={e}^{At}\\,x(0) \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t) & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Next, we find the particular solution. Notice that \n\n$$\n{e}^{A(t-s)}=\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2(t-s)) & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2(t-s)) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2(t-s)) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(2(t-s))\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s) & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2(t-s)) & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2(t-s)) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2(t-s)) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(2(t-s))\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2(t-s)) \\\\ 3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2(t-s))\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{0}^{t}\\begin{bmatrix}3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2(t-s)) \\\\ 3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2(t-s))\\end{bmatrix}\\text{d}s \\\\  & ={\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2(t-s)) \\\\ -\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2(t-s))\\end{bmatrix}}_{s=0}^{s=t} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}3-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t) \\\\ 3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)\\end{bmatrix}+\\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}3-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t) \\\\ 3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)+3 \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)+3 \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186308719 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d9104f75-3823-5343-b10e-35210deee4b1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}(4t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307163}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}(4t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307163} :answer-field/id #uuid "0de54400-c651-59cf-a2eb-bab2e9e63b82" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307571}] :question/id #uuid "411e1067-1bf2-5810-9a74-3f6443bfc23e" :question/math-academy-id "q-335058" :question/problem "$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t) &=4y(t)-4 \\\\ {y}^{′}(t) &=-4x(t),\\end{aligned}\\right.\\,\\begin{bmatrix}x(0) \\\\ y(0)\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the initial value problem above.\n\n*Hint: ${e}^{At}=\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t) & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t)\\end{bmatrix},$ where $A=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 4 \\\\ -4 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.$*\n\n| $\\begin{bmatrix}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{bmatrix}=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t)$ |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "Writing our system in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 4 \\\\ -4 & 0\\end{bmatrix}x(t)+g(t),\n$$\n\nwhere $x(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{bmatrix}$ and $g(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}.$ So, the matrix of the system is $A=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 4 \\\\ -4 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\nGiven the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+g(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, the solution of the initial value problem can be written as the sum of the homogeneous part and a particular solution:\n\n$$\nx(t)={{{e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}\\,x({t}_{0})}_{⏟}}_{\\text{homogeneous part}}+{{{\\int }_{{t}_{0}}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s}_{⏟}}_{\\text{particular solution}},\n$$\n\nwhere $x({t}_{0})$ is the initial condition vector. \n\nLet's evaluate each part separately:\n\n- First, we find the homogeneous part. We are given that \n\n$$\n{e}^{At}=\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t) & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t)\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nSince the initial conditions are given at $t={t}_{0}=0,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})} & ={e}^{At}\\,x(0) \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t) & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t)\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t)+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t)\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Next, we find the particular solution. Notice that \n\n$$\n{e}^{A(t-s)}=\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4(t-s)) & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(4(t-s)) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4(t-s)) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(4(t-s))\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s) & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4(t-s)) & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(4(t-s)) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4(t-s)) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(4(t-s))\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4(t-s)) \\\\ 4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4(t-s))\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{0}^{t}\\begin{bmatrix}-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4(t-s)) \\\\ 4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4(t-s))\\end{bmatrix}\\text{d}s \\\\  & ={\\begin{bmatrix}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4(t-s)) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(4(t-s))\\end{bmatrix}}_{s=0}^{s=t} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t) \\\\ 1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t)\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t)+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t)\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t) \\\\ 1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t)\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t) \\\\ 1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t)\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186308723 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "29953a21-209b-586e-a213-f4a4fa9d67d3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1-{e}^{-t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305546}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1-{e}^{-t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305546} :answer-field/id #uuid "af02c77a-cb82-5db7-8040-47a534b70764" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308078}] :question/id #uuid "47fdaa8b-a137-5a55-9e2b-f6799e375b7a" :question/math-academy-id "q-335081" :question/problem "$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t) &=-x(t)+y(t)+1 \\\\ {y}^{′}(t) &=-y(t),\\end{aligned}\\right.\\,\\begin{bmatrix}x(0) \\\\ y(0)\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the initial value problem above.\n\n*Hint: ${e}^{At}=\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{-t} & t{e}^{-t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{-t}\\end{bmatrix},$ where $A=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}.$*\n\n| $\\begin{bmatrix}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{bmatrix}=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $0$ |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "Writing our system in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}x(t)+g(t),\n$$\n\nwhere $x(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{bmatrix}$ and $g(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}.$ So, the matrix of the system is $A=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\nGiven the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+g(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, the solution of the initial value problem can be written as the sum of the homogeneous part and a particular solution:\n\n$$\nx(t)={{{e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}\\,x({t}_{0})}_{⏟}}_{\\text{homogeneous part}}+{{{\\int }_{{t}_{0}}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s}_{⏟}}_{\\text{particular solution}},\n$$\n\nwhere $x({t}_{0})$ is the initial condition vector. \n\nLet's evaluate each part separately:\n\n- First, we find the homogeneous part. We are given that \n\n$$\n{e}^{At}=\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{-t} & t{e}^{-t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{-t}\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nSince the initial conditions are given at $t={t}_{0}=0,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}x(0) & ={e}^{At}\\,x(0) \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{-t} & t{e}^{-t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{-t}\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Next, we find the particular solution. Notice that \n\n$$\n{e}^{A(t-s)}=\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{-(t-s)} & (t-s){e}^{-(t-s)} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{-(t-s)}\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s) & =\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{-(t-s)} & (t-s){e}^{-(t-s)} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{-(t-s)}\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{-(t-s)} \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{0}^{t}\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{-(t-s)} \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\\text{d}s \\\\  & ={\\begin{bmatrix}-{e}^{-(t-s)} \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}}_{s=0}^{s=t} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1-{e}^{-t} \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}1-{e}^{-t} \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1-{e}^{-t} \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186308724 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c8e79b01-2389-5a91-bd1b-47d545c124e0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{5t}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307021} {:answer/id #uuid "06fe7ba9-e60a-5a45-b758-fa0196ee521e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e^{5t}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186479370}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e^{5t}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186479370} :answer-field/id #uuid "2c1add94-bde4-538a-ae6f-d06b8a3019c5" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307659}] :question/id #uuid "19468931-2ce6-5bd0-af7b-5212e5297c87" :question/math-academy-id "q-335085" :question/problem "$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t) &=5x(t)+y(t)+1 \\\\ {y}^{′}(t) &=5y(t),\\end{aligned}\\right.\\,\\begin{bmatrix}x(0) \\\\ y(0)\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the initial value problem above.\n\n*Hint: ${e}^{At}=\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{5t} & t{e}^{5t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{5t}\\end{bmatrix},$ where $A=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 5\\end{bmatrix}.$*\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"2\">$\\begin{bmatrix}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{bmatrix}=\\frac{1}{5}\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"120px\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0$</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "Writing our system in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 5\\end{bmatrix}x(t)+g(t),\n$$\n\nwhere $x(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{bmatrix}$ and $g(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}.$ So, the matrix of the system is $A=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 5\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\nGiven the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+g(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, the solution of the initial value problem can be written as the sum of the homogeneous part and a particular solution:\n\n$$\nx(t)={{{e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}\\,x({t}_{0})}_{⏟}}_{\\text{homogeneous part}}+{{{\\int }_{{t}_{0}}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s}_{⏟}}_{\\text{particular solution}},\n$$\n\nwhere $x({t}_{0})$ is the initial condition vector. \n\nLet's evaluate each part separately:\n\n- First, we find the homogeneous part. We are given that \n\n$$\n{e}^{At}=\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{5t} & t{e}^{5t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{5t}\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nSince the initial conditions are given at $t={t}_{0}=0,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}x(0) & ={e}^{At}\\,x(0) \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{5t} & t{e}^{5t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{5t}\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Next, we find the particular solution. Notice that \n\n$$\n{e}^{A(t-s)}=\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{5(t-s)} & (t-s){e}^{5(t-s)} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{5(t-s)}\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s) & =\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{5(t-s)} & (t-s){e}^{5(t-s)} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{5(t-s)}\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{5(t-s)} \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{0}^{t}\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{5(t-s)} \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\\text{d}s \\\\  & ={\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{1}{5}{e}^{5(t-s)} \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}}_{s=0}^{s=t} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{5}{e}^{5t}-\\frac{1}{5} \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{5}{e}^{5t}-\\frac{1}{5} \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{5}{e}^{5t}-\\frac{1}{5} \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{5t}-1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186308736 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5f2cc77d-908e-5975-babf-c7e95d32af6b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306066} {:answer/id #uuid "6d657aec-32ba-5cf6-9bf5-c39f0c00dc78" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306197} {:answer/id #uuid "851c1af3-2a69-5a9e-aeb2-bdc919879a73" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306419} {:answer/id #uuid "b970e691-2738-5a66-b02c-0fc82876b459" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306880}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306066} :answer-field/id #uuid "99185d97-eb59-509d-8409-76c2030ce0cc" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308005}] :question/id #uuid "9d6b9f30-3747-520a-a2bd-7bc874e4c993" :question/math-academy-id "q-335127" :question/problem "$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t) &=y(t)+1 \\\\ {y}^{′}(t) &=x(t),\\end{aligned}\\right.\\,\\begin{bmatrix}x(0) \\\\ y(0)\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the initial value problem above.\n\n*Hint: ${e}^{At}=\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(t) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(t) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(t)\\end{bmatrix},$ where $A=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.$*\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"2\">$\\begin{bmatrix}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{bmatrix}=\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"100px\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n</tr><tr>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">$\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(t)-1$</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "Writing our system in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}x(t)+g(t),\n$$\n\nwhere $x(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{bmatrix}$ and $g(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}.$ So, the matrix of the system is $A=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\nGiven the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+g(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, the solution of the initial value problem can be written as the sum of the homogeneous part and a particular solution:\n\n$$\nx(t)={{{e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}\\,x({t}_{0})}_{⏟}}_{\\text{homogeneous part}}+{{{\\int }_{{t}_{0}}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s}_{⏟}}_{\\text{particular solution}},\n$$\n\nwhere $x({t}_{0})$ is the initial condition vector. \n\nLet's evaluate each part separately:\n\n- First, we find the homogeneous part. We are given that \n\n$$\n{e}^{At}=\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(t) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(t) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(t)\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nSince the initial conditions are given at $t={t}_{0}=0,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})} & ={e}^{At}\\,x(0) \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(t) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(t) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(t)\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Next, we find the particular solution. Notice that \n\n$$\n{e}^{A(t-s)}=\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(t-s) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(t-s) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(t-s) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(t-s)\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s) & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(t-s) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(t-s) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(t-s) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(t-s)\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(t-s) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(t-s)\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{0}^{t}\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(t-s) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(t-s)\\end{bmatrix}\\text{d}s \\\\  & ={\\begin{bmatrix}-\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(t-s) \\\\ -\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(t-s)\\end{bmatrix}}_{s=0}^{s=t} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(t) \\\\ \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(t)-1\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(t) \\\\ \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(t)-1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(t) \\\\ \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(t)-1\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186396565 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "445c6a63-f339-5ff2-afa4-e26785fbf1f8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(t)-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396567} {:answer/id #uuid "96de3917-2210-5111-9750-f9437e72cfa5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2t)-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396568} {:answer/id #uuid "875915a9-2dd7-5bfd-a876-9d427aa8a55b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2t)+1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396569} {:answer/id #uuid "ba2a0cc9-e777-59ad-9b3f-6332bbbb90e0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(t)+1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396570}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2t)-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396568} :answer-field/id #uuid "7e1c7d9a-e955-5ffd-bbe8-c5635e09bdc8" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396566}] :question/id #uuid "d2b8ad61-9b47-5971-9495-e31b2ea4691b" :question/math-academy-id "q-335175" :question/problem "$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t) &=2y(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t) &=2x(t)+2,\\end{aligned}\\right.\\,\\begin{bmatrix}x(0) \\\\ y(0)\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the initial value problem above.\n\n*Hint: ${e}^{At}=\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2t) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2t) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2t)\\end{bmatrix},$ where $A=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.$*\n\n| $\\begin{bmatrix}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{bmatrix}=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2t)$ |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "Writing our system in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{bmatrix}x(t)+g(t),\n$$\n\nwhere $x(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{bmatrix}$ and $g(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}.$ So, the matrix of the system is $A=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\nGiven the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+g(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, the solution of the initial value problem can be written as the sum of the homogeneous part and a particular solution:\n\n$$\nx(t)={{{e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}\\,x({t}_{0})}_{⏟}}_{\\text{homogeneous part}}+{{{\\int }_{{t}_{0}}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s}_{⏟}}_{\\text{particular solution}},\n$$\n\nwhere $x({t}_{0})$ is the initial condition vector. \n\nLet's evaluate each part separately:\n\n- First, we find the homogeneous part. We are given that \n\n$$\n{e}^{At}=\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2t) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2t) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2t)\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nSince the initial conditions are given at $t={t}_{0}=0,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})} & ={e}^{At}\\,x(0) \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2t) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2t) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2t)\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Next, we find the particular solution. Notice that \n\n$$\n{e}^{A(t-s)}=\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2(t-s)) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2(t-s)) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2(t-s)) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2(t-s))\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s) & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2(t-s)) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2(t-s)) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2(t-s)) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2(t-s))\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}2\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2(t-s)) \\\\ 2\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2(t-s))\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{0}^{t}\\begin{bmatrix}2\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2(t-s)) \\\\ 2\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2(t-s))\\end{bmatrix}\\text{d}s \\\\  & ={\\begin{bmatrix}-\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2(t-s)) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2(t-s))\\end{bmatrix}}_{s=0}^{s=t} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2t)-1 \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2t)\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2t)-1 \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2t)\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2t)-1 \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2t)\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186396729 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "556a1d6d-0b97-5b9c-919a-ffcaef348e99" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(7t)+1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396731} {:answer/id #uuid "47177d5f-d60d-5a76-a622-4448eaae8c59" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(7t)-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396732} {:answer/id #uuid "7b9b3be8-96e2-584f-b6b0-e44dcfa5b59f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(7t)+1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396733} {:answer/id #uuid "5e17787c-fdb3-5dc6-9f7d-ad11c18b5f0b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(7t)-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396734}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(7t)-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396734} :answer-field/id #uuid "0c3839e0-7572-5b48-a67f-8007a8d31b72" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396730}] :question/id #uuid "9ba8d18b-c5fe-5645-a494-a8fce82f879d" :question/math-academy-id "q-335183" :question/problem "$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t) &=7y(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t) &=7x(t)+7,\\end{aligned}\\right.\\,\\begin{bmatrix}x(0) \\\\ y(0)\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the initial value problem above.\n\n*Hint: ${e}^{At}=\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(7t) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(7t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(7t) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(7t)\\end{bmatrix},$ where $A=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 7 \\\\ 7 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.$*\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"2\">$\\begin{bmatrix}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{bmatrix}=\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"80px\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n</tr><tr>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">$\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(7t)$</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "Writing our system in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 7 \\\\ 7 & 0\\end{bmatrix}x(t)+g(t),\n$$\n\nwhere $x(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{bmatrix}$ and $g(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix}.$ So, the matrix of the system is $A=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 7 \\\\ 7 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\nGiven the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+g(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, the solution of the initial value problem can be written as the sum of the homogeneous part and a particular solution:\n\n$$\nx(t)={{{e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}\\,x({t}_{0})}_{⏟}}_{\\text{homogeneous part}}+{{{\\int }_{{t}_{0}}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s}_{⏟}}_{\\text{particular solution}},\n$$\n\nwhere $x({t}_{0})$ is the initial condition vector. \n\nLet's evaluate each part separately:\n\n- First, we find the homogeneous part. We are given that \n\n$$\n{e}^{At}=\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(7t) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(7t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(7t) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(7t)\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nSince the initial conditions are given at $t={t}_{0}=0,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})} & ={e}^{At}\\,x(0) \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(7t) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(7t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(7t) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(7t)\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Next, we find the particular solution. Notice that \n\n$$\n{e}^{A(t-s)}=\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(7(t-s)) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(7(t-s)) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(7(t-s)) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(7(t-s))\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s) & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(7(t-s)) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(7(t-s)) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(7(t-s)) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(7(t-s))\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}7\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(7(t-s)) \\\\ 7\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(7(t-s))\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{0}^{t}\\begin{bmatrix}7\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(7(t-s)) \\\\ 7\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(7(t-s))\\end{bmatrix}\\text{d}s \\\\  & ={\\begin{bmatrix}-\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(7(t-s)) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(7(t-s))\\end{bmatrix}}_{s=0}^{s=t} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(7t)-1 \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(7t)\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(7t)-1 \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(7t)\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(7t)-1 \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(7t)\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186495074 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c02e4fa5-edc3-5680-b383-eb861b94c2ae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(7t)-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494771}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(7t)-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494771} :answer-field/id #uuid "8e66a9d5-c3d1-5ab6-8270-3abb2df59cb7" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494982}] :question/id #uuid "30dbc074-1ece-5bdf-8ee0-957449e10161" :question/math-academy-id "q-335068" :question/problem "$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t) &=7y(t)+7 \\\\ {y}^{′}(t) &=-7x(t),\\end{aligned}\\right.\\,\\begin{bmatrix}x(0) \\\\ y(0)\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the initial value problem above.\n\n*Hint: ${e}^{At}=\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(7t) & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(7t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(7t) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(7t)\\end{bmatrix},$ where $A=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 7 \\\\ -7 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.$*\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"2\">$\\begin{bmatrix}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{bmatrix}=\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"120px\">$2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(7t)$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "Writing our system in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 7 \\\\ -7 & 0\\end{bmatrix}x(t)+g(t),\n$$\n\nwhere $x(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{bmatrix}$ and $g(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}7 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}.$ So, the matrix of the system is $A=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 7 \\\\ -7 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\nGiven the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+g(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, the solution of the initial value problem can be written as the sum of the homogeneous part and a particular solution:\n\n$$\nx(t)={{{e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}\\,x({t}_{0})}_{⏟}}_{\\text{homogeneous part}}+{{{\\int }_{{t}_{0}}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s}_{⏟}}_{\\text{particular solution}},\n$$\n\nwhere $x({t}_{0})$ is the initial condition vector. \n\nLet's evaluate each part separately:\n\n- First, we find the homogeneous part. We are given that \n\n$$\n{e}^{At}=\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(7t) & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(7t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(7t) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(7t)\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nSince the initial conditions are given at $t={t}_{0}=0,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})} & ={e}^{At}\\,x(0) \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(7t) & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(7t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(7t) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(7t)\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(7t) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(7t)\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Next, we find the particular solution. Notice that \n\n$$\n{e}^{A(t-s)}=\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(7(t-s)) & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(7(t-s)) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(7(t-s)) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(7(t-s))\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s) & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(7(t-s)) & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(7(t-s)) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(7(t-s)) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(7(t-s))\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}7 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}7\\operatorname{cos}⁡(7(t-s)) \\\\ -7\\operatorname{sin}⁡(7(t-s))\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{0}^{t}\\begin{bmatrix}7\\operatorname{cos}⁡(7(t-s)) \\\\ -7\\operatorname{sin}⁡(7(t-s))\\end{bmatrix}\\text{d}s \\\\  & ={\\begin{bmatrix}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(7(t-s)) \\\\ -\\operatorname{cos}⁡(7(t-s))\\end{bmatrix}}_{s=0}^{s=t} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(7t) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(7t)-1\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(7t) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(7t)\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(7t) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(7t)-1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(7t) \\\\ 2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(7t)-1\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186495161 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6b596b99-7294-5ff0-b898-15ee8d9ff660" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(4t)+1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494537} {:answer/id #uuid "a547dde1-3353-563d-9dc4-c26608fe2262" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(4t)-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494695} {:answer/id #uuid "cd1db945-1bea-566f-ac8f-8accdd99a0c5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(4t)+1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494803} {:answer/id #uuid "e10e0aba-3ff2-54c6-8ed9-ecc46df06c76" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(4t)-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494853}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(4t)-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494695} :answer-field/id #uuid "7f5cfcb1-f43f-54aa-937a-52c96207e17b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494976}] :question/id #uuid "e9f770d5-4f03-58ec-b9ae-bcbaf7705c59" :question/math-academy-id "q-335166" :question/problem "$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t) &=4y(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t) &=4x(t)+4,\\end{aligned}\\right.\\,\\begin{bmatrix}x(0) \\\\ y(0)\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the initial value problem above.\n\n*Hint: ${e}^{At}=\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(4t) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(4t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(4t) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(4t)\\end{bmatrix},$ where $A=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 4 \\\\ 4 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.$*\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"2\">$\\begin{bmatrix}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{bmatrix}=\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"80px\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n</tr><tr>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">$\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(4t)$</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "Writing our system in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 4 \\\\ 4 & 0\\end{bmatrix}x(t)+g(t),\n$$\n\nwhere $x(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{bmatrix}$ and $g(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}.$ So, the matrix of the system is $A=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 4 \\\\ 4 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\nGiven the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+g(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, the solution of the initial value problem can be written as the sum of the homogeneous part and a particular solution:\n\n$$\nx(t)={{{e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}\\,x({t}_{0})}_{⏟}}_{\\text{homogeneous part}}+{{{\\int }_{{t}_{0}}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s}_{⏟}}_{\\text{particular solution}},\n$$\n\nwhere $x({t}_{0})$ is the initial condition vector. \n\nLet's evaluate each part separately:\n\n- First, we find the homogeneous part. We are given that \n\n$$\n{e}^{At}=\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(4t) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(4t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(4t) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(4t)\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nSince the initial conditions are given at $t={t}_{0}=0,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})} & ={e}^{At}\\,x(0) \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(4t) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(4t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(4t) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(4t)\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Next, we find the particular solution. Notice that \n\n$$\n{e}^{A(t-s)}=\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(4(t-s)) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(4(t-s)) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(4(t-s)) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(4(t-s))\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s) & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(4(t-s)) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(4(t-s)) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(4(t-s)) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(4(t-s))\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}4\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(4(t-s)) \\\\ 4\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(4(t-s))\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{0}^{t}\\begin{bmatrix}4\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(4(t-s)) \\\\ 4\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(4(t-s))\\end{bmatrix}\\text{d}s \\\\  & ={\\begin{bmatrix}-\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(4(t-s)) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(4(t-s))\\end{bmatrix}}_{s=0}^{s=t} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(4t)-1 \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(4t)\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(4t)-1 \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(4t)\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(4t)-1 \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(4t)\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186512909 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4b374613-ddcc-5c32-8993-19ba069fb8ec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e^{4t}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512258}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e^{4t}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512258} :answer-field/id #uuid "083c749e-9d27-588e-b8bf-03bf5d6d7291" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512725}] :question/id #uuid "8c12baec-9a09-54f7-8159-4ab5ea602070" :question/math-academy-id "q-335084" :question/problem "$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t) &=4x(t)+y(t)+2 \\\\ {y}^{′}(t) &=4y(t),\\end{aligned}\\right.\\,[\\begin{aligned}x(0) \\\\ y(0)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the initial value problem above.\n\n*Hint: ${e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{4t} & t{e}^{4t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{4t}\\end{aligned}],$ where $A=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{aligned}].$*\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"2\">$[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}]=\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"120px\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0$</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "Writing our system in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{aligned}]x(t)+g(t),\n$$\n\nwhere $x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}]$ and $g(t)=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].$ So, the matrix of the system is $A=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{aligned}].$\n\nGiven the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+g(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, the solution of the initial value problem can be written as the sum of the homogeneous part and a particular solution:\n\n$$\nx(t)={{{e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}\\,x({t}_{0})}_{⏟}}_{\\text{homogeneous part}}+{{{\\int }_{{t}_{0}}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s}_{⏟}}_{\\text{particular solution}},\n$$\n\nwhere $x({t}_{0})$ is the initial condition vector. \n\nLet's evaluate each part separately:\n\n- First, we find the homogeneous part. We are given that \n\n$$\n{e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{4t} & t{e}^{4t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{4t}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSince the initial conditions are given at $t={t}_{0}=0,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}x(0) & ={e}^{At}\\,x(0) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{4t} & t{e}^{4t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{4t}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Next, we find the particular solution. Notice that \n\n$$\n{e}^{A(t-s)}=[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{4(t-s)} & (t-s){e}^{4(t-s)} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{4(t-s)}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s) & =[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{4(t-s)} & (t-s){e}^{4(t-s)} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{4(t-s)}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2{e}^{4(t-s)} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{0}^{t}[\\begin{aligned}2{e}^{4(t-s)} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\text{d}s \\\\  & ={[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{4(t-s)} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}_{s=0}^{s=t} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{4t}-\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{4t}-\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{4t}-\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{4t}-1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186512943 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a13ebe21-3fd3-5659-96f0-dac3aebbcdb5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-e^{2t}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512473}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-e^{2t}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512473} :answer-field/id #uuid "6115237a-ca95-5556-91b1-d22bf91c2c37" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512779}] :question/id #uuid "d29ce693-46aa-5cb5-a64c-988886b4e7a0" :question/math-academy-id "q-335072" :question/problem "$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t) &=2x(t)+y(t)+1 \\\\ {y}^{′}(t) &=2y(t),\\end{aligned}\\right.\\,[\\begin{aligned}x(0) \\\\ y(0)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the initial value problem above.\n\n*Hint: ${e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{2t} & t{e}^{2t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}],$ where $A=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}].$*\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"2\">$[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}]=\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"80px\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0$</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "Writing our system in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]x(t)+g(t),\n$$\n\nwhere $x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}]$ and $g(t)=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].$ So, the matrix of the system is $A=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}].$\n\nGiven the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+g(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, the solution of the initial value problem can be written as the sum of the homogeneous part and a particular solution:\n\n$$\nx(t)={{{e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}\\,x({t}_{0})}_{⏟}}_{\\text{homogeneous part}}+{{{\\int }_{{t}_{0}}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s}_{⏟}}_{\\text{particular solution}},\n$$\n\nwhere $x({t}_{0})$ is the initial condition vector. \n\nLet's evaluate each part separately:\n\n- First, we find the homogeneous part. We are given that \n\n$$\n{e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{2t} & t{e}^{2t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSince the initial conditions are given at $t={t}_{0}=0,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})} & ={e}^{At}\\,x(0) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{2t} & t{e}^{2t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-{e}^{2t} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Next, we find the particular solution. Notice that \n\n$$\n{e}^{A(t-s)}=[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{2(t-s)} & (t-s){e}^{2(t-s)} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{2(t-s)}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s) & =[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{2(t-s)} & (t-s){e}^{2(t-s)} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{2(t-s)}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{2(t-s)} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{0}^{t}[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{2(t-s)} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\text{d}s \\\\  & ={[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{2(t-s)} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}_{s=0}^{s=t} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{2t}-\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}-{e}^{2t} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{2t}-\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{2t}-\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}-{e}^{2t}-1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}-{e}^{2t}-1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186512945 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2ce80ed6-c2fb-573a-bcb7-17c24ee2cd02" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1-e^{-t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512202}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1-e^{-t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512202} :answer-field/id #uuid "7d8ad94d-1b6b-50f4-917b-e60fcda59e4c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512794}] :question/id #uuid "dcde9f99-5a2a-52a5-a122-c3ef3631c507" :question/math-academy-id "q-335070" :question/problem "$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t) &=-x(t)+y(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t) &=-y(t)+1,\\end{aligned}\\right.\\,[\\begin{aligned}x(0) \\\\ y(0)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the initial value problem above.\n\n*Hint: ${e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-t} & t{e}^{-t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{-t}\\end{aligned}],$ where $A=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}].$*\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"2\">$[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}]=\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"80px\">$1-{e}^{-t}-t{e}^{-t}$ </td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "Writing our system in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]x(t)+g(t),\n$$\n\nwhere $x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}]$ and $g(t)=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$ So, the matrix of the system is $A=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}].$\n\nGiven the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+g(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, the solution of the initial value problem can be written as the sum of the homogeneous part and a particular solution:\n\n$$\nx(t)={{{e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}\\,x({t}_{0})}_{⏟}}_{\\text{homogeneous part}}+{{{\\int }_{{t}_{0}}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s}_{⏟}}_{\\text{particular solution}},\n$$\n\nwhere $x({t}_{0})$ is the initial condition vector. \n\nLet's evaluate each part separately:\n\n- First, we find the homogeneous part. We are given that \n\n$$\n{e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-t} & t{e}^{-t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{-t}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSince the initial conditions are given at $t={t}_{0}=0,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})} & ={e}^{At}\\,x(0) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-t} & t{e}^{-t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{-t}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Next, we find the particular solution. Notice that \n\n$$\n{e}^{A(t-s)}=[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-(t-s)} & (t-s){e}^{-(t-s)} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{-(t-s)}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s) & =[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-(t-s)} & (t-s){e}^{-(t-s)} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{-(t-s)}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}(t-s){e}^{s-t} \\\\ {e}^{s-t}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{0}^{t}[\\begin{aligned}(t-s){e}^{s-t} \\\\ {e}^{s-t}\\end{aligned}]\\text{d}s \\\\  & ={[\\begin{aligned}(-s+t+1){e}^{s-t} \\\\ {e}^{s-t}\\end{aligned}]}_{s=0}^{s=t} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1-(t+1){e}^{-t} \\\\ 1-{e}^{-t}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}1-(t+1){e}^{-t} \\\\ 1-{e}^{-t}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1-{e}^{-t}-t{e}^{-t} \\\\ 1-{e}^{-t}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186535950 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d4f64bf3-528b-508d-afe7-7fb41040696f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\cos(t)-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186535760}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\cos(t)-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186535760} :answer-field/id #uuid "c0cddfae-ecf5-50fd-9bfc-04c2102bb55f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186535905}] :question/id #uuid "5cb555db-6a59-509d-947e-27c4f1a2a7e6" :question/math-academy-id "q-335062" :question/problem "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)=y(t)+1 \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)=-x(t),\\end{aligned}\\,[\\begin{aligned}x(0) \\\\ y(0)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the initial value problem above.\n\n*Hint: ${e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t) & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)\\end{aligned}],$ where $A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}].$*\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"2\">$[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}]=\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"120px\">$2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t)$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "Writing our system in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}]x(t)+g(t),\n$$\n\nwhere $x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}]$ and $g(t)=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].$ So, the matrix of the system is $A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}].$\n\nGiven the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+g(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, the solution of the initial value problem can be written as the sum of the homogeneous part and a particular solution:\n\n$$\nx(t)={{{e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}\\,x({t}_{0})}_{⏟}}_{\\text{homogeneous part}}+{{{\\int }_{{t}_{0}}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s}_{⏟}}_{\\text{particular solution}},\n$$\n\nwhere $x({t}_{0})$ is the initial condition vector. \n\nLet's evaluate each part separately:\n\n- First, we find the homogeneous part. We are given that \n\n$$\n{e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t) & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSince the initial conditions are given at $t={t}_{0}=0,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})} & ={e}^{At}\\,x(0) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t) & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Next, we find the particular solution. Notice that \n\n$$\n{e}^{A(t-s)}=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t-s) & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(t-s) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t-s) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(t-s)\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t-s) & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(t-s) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t-s) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(t-s)\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t-s) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t-s)\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{0}^{t}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t-s) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t-s)\\end{aligned}]\\text{d}s \\\\  & ={[\\begin{aligned}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t-s) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(t-s)\\end{aligned}]}_{s=0}^{s=t} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)-1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)-1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t) \\\\ 2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)-1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Solving an Inhomogeneous System Using a Given Matrix Exponential"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186229133 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186228915 :question/id #uuid "c24150ed-748b-5069-9fc5-48d4e6deaef2" :question/math-academy-id "e-21721" :question/problem "Consider the inhomogeneous system  $\\mathbf{x}'(t)=A\\mathbf{x}(t)+\\mathbf{g}(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix. A derivation of the formula for the solution $\\mathbf{x}(t)$ passing through $\\mathbf{x}(t_0)$ is presented below.\n\n$\\textrm{L1}{:}\\;$ Let $\\mathbf{y}(t)=e^{-A(t-t_0)}\\mathbf{x}(t)$  \n\n$\\textrm{L2}{:}\\;$ $\\mathbf{y}'(t) = -Ae^{-A(t-t_0)}\\mathbf{x}(t) + e^{-A(t-t_0)}\\mathbf{x}'(t)$  \n\n$\\textrm{L3}{:}\\;$ $\\mathbf{y}'(t)=e^{-A(t-t_0)}\\mathbf{g}(t)$  \n\n$\\textrm{L4}{:}\\;$ $\\displaystyle\\mathbf{y}(t)-\\mathbf{y}(t_0) = \\int_{t_0}^{t} e^{-A(s-t_0)}\\mathbf{g}(s) \\, \\text{d}s$\n\n$\\textrm{L5}{:}\\;$ $\\mathbf{y}(t_0)=\\mathbf{x}(t_0)$ \n\n$\\textrm{L6}{:}\\;$ $\\displaystyle\\mathbf{y}(t)=\\mathbf{x}(t_0)+\\int_{t_0}^{t} e^{-A(s-t_0)}\\mathbf{g}(s) \\, \\text{d}s$  \n\n$\\textrm{L7}{:}\\;$ $\\displaystyle e^{A(t-t_0)}\\mathbf{y}(t)=e^{A(t-t_0)}\\mathbf{x}(t_0)+\\int_{t_0}^{t} e^{A(t-s)}\\mathbf{g}(s) \\, \\text{d}s$\n\n$\\textrm{L8}{:}\\;$ $e^{A(t-t_0)}\\mathbf{y}(t)=\\mathbf{x}(t)$\n\n$\\textrm{L9}{:}\\;$ $\\displaystyle\\mathbf{x}(t)=e^{A(t-t_0)}\\mathbf{x}(t_0)+\\int_{t_0}^{t} e^{A(t-s)}\\mathbf{g}(s) \\, \\text{d}s$\n\nFill in the blanks with the correct reasons to justify each step of the reasoning.\n\n$\\quad$ Line $\\textrm{L3}$ follows from $\\textrm{L2}$ by  ![](images/a5/a57b16a4b4392ad68547e3192dfde0c795d11e960c5100e14cd54c275df18415.svg).\n\n$\\quad$ Line $\\textrm{L5}$ follows from line $\\textrm{L1}$ by ![](images/28/281de511438021a8e37a938beb7039bb060a44f944da15128634c8a037f9830e.svg).\n\n$\\quad$ Line $\\textrm{L8}$ follows from line $\\textrm{L1}$ by ![](images/62/62aae06fe282decc2963be0ca8d0018b30fac355624b46226e93d27033a6e2e2.svg)." :question/worked-solution "Let's justify each of the selected steps.\n\n- We first consider lines $\\textrm{L2}$ and $\\textrm{L3}.$ Starting from\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{y}'(t) = -Ae^{-A(t-t_0)}\\mathbf{x}(t) + e^{-A(t-t_0)}\\mathbf{x}'(t)\n$$\n\nin $\\textrm{L2}$ and substituting $\\mathbf{x}'(t)=A\\mathbf{x}(t)+\\mathbf{g}(t)$ from the original system gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}(t) & =-A{e}^{-A(t-{t}_{0})}x(t)+{e}^{-A(t-{t}_{0})}(Ax(t)+g(t)) \\\\  & =-A{e}^{-A(t-{t}_{0})}x(t)+A{e}^{-A(t-{t}_{0})}x(t)+{e}^{-A(t-{t}_{0})}g(t) \\\\  & ={e}^{-A(t-{t}_{0})}g(t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, $\\textrm{L3}$ follows from $\\textrm{L2}$ by ![](images/83/83729359deb05033193c0efafb53f3d3164d7974543a2549eb63276bbd834311.svg)\n\n- Next, we consider lines $\\textrm{L1}$ and $\\textrm{L5}.$ Evaluating $\\mathbf{y}(t)=e^{-A(t-t_0)}\\mathbf{x}(t)$ at $t=t_0$ gives\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{y}(t_0)=e^{-A(t_0-t_0)}\\mathbf{x}(t_0)=I\\mathbf{x}(t_0)=\\mathbf{x}(t_0).\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\textrm{L5}$ follows from line $\\textrm{L1}$  by ![](images/7e/7e6ad910e9037e26dc2fd533bbab660b6c6f90e48b05975b071390d6063a9219.svg)\n\n- Finally, we consider lines $\\textrm{L1}$ and $\\textrm{L8}.$ Multiplying both sides of\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{y}(t)=e^{-A(t-t_0)}\\mathbf{x}(t)\n$$\n\nfrom $\\textrm{L1}$ by $e^{A(t-t_0)}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}y(t) & ={e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}{e}^{-A(t-{t}_{0})}x(t) \\\\  & =x(t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\textrm{L8}$ follows from $\\textrm{L1}$ by ![](images/75/759ebf5f590b98c90b82384ce915060a412eeb20af8f9fe0949dacb9a1b9980f.svg)"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4c4b78fa-76af-5261-87a0-d1960aa0fe04" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186229662 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "043cab10-8cca-5c28-8590-64e902b215cb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "evaluating at $t=0$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305190} {:answer/id #uuid "2e0f1c6a-48c2-5432-a68a-0bfc1b52f410" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "adding ${e}^{At}x(0)$ to both sides" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305591} {:answer/id #uuid "e1193063-7341-5592-80b6-f049092b5118" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "multiplying both sides by ${e}^{At}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307235} {:answer/id #uuid "fe1e5ae0-1095-5c04-a177-ec89e8a2fa83" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "differentiating and using the sum rule" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307497}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "multiplying both sides by ${e}^{At}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307235} :answer-field/id #uuid "059c975e-41cb-532c-8945-357ffa2f3233" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307541} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "99f1fcac-955c-5d3a-aaf1-1ec9a2ad59a6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{L3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306588} {:answer/id #uuid "c2c44ffd-44d9-5523-8a9d-00ef9a2bd461" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{L1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306967} {:answer/id #uuid "f50a4a3b-7800-51b9-895b-5c1203c635c1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{L2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307420}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{L3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306588} :answer-field/id #uuid "11d78e4b-0e31-5dc3-88f6-eaaca60eaaee" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307578} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "29352c27-ddf5-57b3-990d-1ef83ab447b2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "applying a change of variables" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305538} {:answer/id #uuid "6c48cb3b-9f66-5d9e-9b72-cd5eae530d9d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "substituting ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+g(t)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306189} {:answer/id #uuid "b47698e0-4356-549f-a758-5149484e0793" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "differentiating and using the product rule" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306844} {:answer/id #uuid "e613b8f2-cac3-5d0e-9c09-f67cb9812261" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "evaluating at $t=0$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307280}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "differentiating and using the product rule" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306844} :answer-field/id #uuid "35c5d74f-7249-58a1-9988-dac7f198a8ca" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307690} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "61d8ddbb-a246-5b6a-950e-2e94bc4f44f4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306097} {:answer/id #uuid "7787152c-6a4b-5157-84eb-dbd4a526b25d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "s" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306285} {:answer/id #uuid "a09cde25-0e67-5fd7-844f-05cf13d075ed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306655} {:answer/id #uuid "a5bfb069-1f0d-5d66-8b80-0635f203dd16" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306712}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306712} :answer-field/id #uuid "e4fb121a-87b2-5587-adc2-c65edcd5e58d" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308242}] :question/id #uuid "3d5aa81c-82a3-50e6-9a6f-bc0b6662f32d" :question/math-academy-id "q-334533" :question/problem "Consider the inhomogeneous system  ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+g(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix. A derivation of the formula for the solution $x(t)$ passing through $x(0)$ is presented below.\n\n$\\text{L1}:\\,$ Let $y(t)={e}^{-At}x(t)$  \n\n$\\text{L2}:\\,$ ${y}^{′}(t)=-A{e}^{-At}x(t)+{e}^{-At}{x}^{′}(t)$  \n\n$\\text{L3}:\\,$ ${y}^{′}(t)={e}^{-At}g(t)$  \n\n$\\text{L4}:\\,$ $y(t)-y(0)={\\int }_{0}^{t}{e}^{-As}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s$\n\n$\\text{L5}:\\,$ $y(0)=x(0)$ \n\n$\\text{L6}:\\,$ $y(t)=x(0)+{\\int }_{0}^{t}{e}^{-As}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s$  \n\n$\\text{L7}:\\,$ ${e}^{At}y(t)={e}^{At}x(0)+{\\int }_{0}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s$\n\n$\\text{L8}:\\,$ ${e}^{At}y(t)=x(t)$\n\n$\\text{L9}:\\,$ $x(t)={e}^{At}x(0)+{\\int }_{0}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s$\n\nSelect the correct options to justify each step of the reasoning.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L2}$ follows from $\\text{L1}$ by  \n{{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L4}$ follows from line\n{{field-2}}\nby integrating both sides from $0$ to \n{{field-3}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L7}$ follows from line $\\text{L6}$ by  \n{{field-4}}." :question/worked-solution "Let's justify each of the selected steps.\n\n- We first consider lines $\\text{L1}$ and $\\text{L2}.$ Differentiating $y(t)={e}^{-At}x(t)$ and applying the product rule gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}(t) & =({e}^{-At})^{′}x(t)+{e}^{-At}{x}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =(-A){e}^{-At}x(t)+{e}^{-At}{x}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =-A{e}^{-At}x(t)+{e}^{-At}{x}^{′}(t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, $\\text{L2}$ follows from $\\text{L1}$ by $\\text{differentiating and using the product rule}.$\n\n- Next, we consider lines $\\text{L3}$ and $\\text{L4}.$ Integrating ${y}^{′}(t)={e}^{-At}g(t)$ from $0$ to $t$ in $\\text{L3}$ yields\n\n$$\ny(t)-y(0)={\\int }_{0}^{t}{e}^{-As}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s.\n$$\n\nSo, $\\text{L4}$ follows from $\\text{L3}$ by integrating both sides from $0$ to $t.$\n\n- Finally, we consider lines $\\text{L6}$ and $\\text{L7}.$ Multiplying both sides of\n\n$$\ny(t)=x(0)+{\\int }_{0}^{t}{e}^{-As}g(s)\\,ds\n$$\n\nfrom $\\text{L6}$ by ${e}^{At}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{At}y(t) & ={e}^{At}x(0)+{e}^{At}{\\int }_{0}^{t}{e}^{-As}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s \\\\  & ={e}^{At}x(0)+{\\int }_{0}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\text{L7}$ follows from $\\text{L6}$ by $\\text{multiplying both sides by }{e}^{At}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186229683 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c189b4b8-e649-59af-816a-a0162eba91e3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}y(t)=x(t)+{t}_{0}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370351} {:answer/id #uuid "794bd4e3-c940-5f5b-ac2e-7bed9c9fda49" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y({t}_{0})=x({t}_{0})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370352} {:answer/id #uuid "39704c3f-642f-5f72-adf4-ba19d22ad47c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y(t)={e}^{-A(t-{t}_{0})}x(t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370353} {:answer/id #uuid "c17dbc31-0ce1-56f2-b44e-655f25c7dc56" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+g(t)+{t}_{0}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370354}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y({t}_{0})=x({t}_{0})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370352} :answer-field/id #uuid "fda6ab81-45b1-5bf1-8ab0-0c01e2051850" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370350} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "782fb0a5-ca2e-5b95-b112-f1d6b4541b99" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "applying a change of variables" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370356} {:answer/id #uuid "9f55c8c5-2761-513a-a8db-cb284e8363cd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "substituting ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+g(t)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370357} {:answer/id #uuid "a540c6e8-5cf1-5239-b2ce-b9c0f9305221" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "evaluating at $t={t}_{0}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370358} {:answer/id #uuid "b377ec22-52b4-5ba4-8938-f3e674edaf05" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "substituting ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+g(t)+{t}_{0}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370359}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "substituting ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+g(t)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370357} :answer-field/id #uuid "0ac2465d-1b6b-571f-8ad5-f676311eecc3" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370355} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b22b0068-c91e-5e17-8273-d57a23e8cd99" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "multiplying both sides by ${e}^{A(t+{t}_{0})}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370361} {:answer/id #uuid "fa56956d-8433-5ed4-a9ab-5ad87b36fc9a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "multiplying both sides by ${e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370362} {:answer/id #uuid "b22a80df-cabc-55d1-8e1f-bc6b7bbbf967" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "integrating both sides" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370363} {:answer/id #uuid "313b72e4-fa0c-5a28-b44f-976590cf94a4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "evaluating at $t={t}_{0}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370364}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "multiplying both sides by ${e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370362} :answer-field/id #uuid "3d14676a-3691-59df-99bb-47536c494327" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370360} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a9c023ba-2eac-5882-bb4b-6510e186b4d3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{L1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370366} {:answer/id #uuid "a6bc1038-64cb-535a-b633-b2c5e10b6ad4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{L4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370367} {:answer/id #uuid "18d5edcb-dfe6-5a62-8079-1480a5dfcf7b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{L3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370368}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{L4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370367} :answer-field/id #uuid "d3847361-a50f-5b4d-82d7-e69b36f4a78c" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370365}] :question/id #uuid "de398203-cf28-58bc-baf8-d4c0b37651f0" :question/math-academy-id "q-335416" :question/problem "Consider the inhomogeneous system  ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+g(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix. A derivation of the formula for the solution $x(t)$ passing through $x({t}_{0})$ is presented below.\n\n$\\text{L1}:\\,$ Let $y(t)={e}^{-A(t-{t}_{0})}x(t)$  \n\n$\\text{L2}:\\,$ ${y}^{′}(t)=-A{e}^{-A(t-{t}_{0})}x(t)+{e}^{-A(t-{t}_{0})}{x}^{′}(t)$  \n\n$\\text{L3}:\\,$ ${y}^{′}(t)={e}^{-A(t-{t}_{0})}g(t)$  \n\n$\\text{L4}:\\,$ $y(t)-y({t}_{0})={\\int }_{{t}_{0}}^{t}{e}^{-A(s-{t}_{0})}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s$\n\n$\\text{L5}:\\,$ $y({t}_{0})=x({t}_{0})$ \n\n$\\text{L6}:\\,$ $y(t)=x({t}_{0})+{\\int }_{{t}_{0}}^{t}{e}^{-A(s-{t}_{0})}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s$  \n\n$\\text{L7}:\\,$ ${e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}y(t)={e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}x({t}_{0})+{\\int }_{{t}_{0}}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s$\n\n$\\text{L8}:\\,$ ${e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}y(t)=x(t)$\n\n$\\text{L9}:\\,$ $x(t)={e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}x({t}_{0})+{\\int }_{{t}_{0}}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s$\n\nSelect the correct options to justify each step of the reasoning.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L3}$ follows from $\\text{L2}$ by  \n{{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L6}$ follows from line\n{{field-2}}\nby substituting \n{{field-3}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L8}$ follows from line $\\text{L1}$ by  \n{{field-4}}." :question/worked-solution "Let's justify each of the selected steps.\n\n- We first consider lines $\\text{L2}$ and $\\text{L3}.$ Starting from\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}(t)=-A{e}^{-A(t-{t}_{0})}x(t)+{e}^{-A(t-{t}_{0})}{x}^{′}(t)\n$$\n\nin $\\text{L2}$ and substituting ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+g(t)$ from the original system gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}(t) & =-A{e}^{-A(t-{t}_{0})}x(t)+{e}^{-A(t-{t}_{0})}(Ax(t)+g(t)) \\\\  & =-A{e}^{-A(t-{t}_{0})}x(t)+A{e}^{-A(t-{t}_{0})}x(t)+{e}^{-A(t-{t}_{0})}g(t) \\\\  & ={e}^{-A(t-{t}_{0})}g(t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, $\\text{L3}$ follows from $\\text{L2}$ by $\\text{substituting }{x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+g(t).$\n\n- Next, we consider lines $\\text{L4}$, $\\text{L5}$, and $\\text{L6}.$ From $\\text{L4}$ we have\n\n$$\ny(t)-y({t}_{0})={\\int }_{{t}_{0}}^{t}{e}^{-A(s-{t}_{0})}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s.\n$$\n\nUsing $y({t}_{0})=x({t}_{0})$ from $\\text{L5}$, this becomes\n\n$$\ny(t)-x({t}_{0})={\\int }_{{t}_{0}}^{t}{e}^{-A(s-{t}_{0})}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s,\n$$\n\nso\n\n$$\ny(t)=x({t}_{0})+{\\int }_{{t}_{0}}^{t}{e}^{-A(s-{t}_{0})}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s.\n$$\n\nThus, $\\text{L6}$ follows from $\\text{L4}$ by substituting $y({t}_{0})=x({t}_{0}).$\n\n- Finally, we consider lines $\\text{L1}$ and $\\text{L8}.$ Multiplying both sides of\n\n$$\ny(t)={e}^{-A(t-{t}_{0})}x(t)\n$$\n\nfrom $\\text{L1}$ by ${e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}y(t) & ={e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}{e}^{-A(t-{t}_{0})}x(t) \\\\  & =x(t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\text{L8}$ follows from $\\text{L1}$ by $\\text{multiplying both sides by }{e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186311584 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "16a95f78-5388-52c8-81fd-1590793a0892" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{L2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308923} {:answer/id #uuid "458cdaa3-94ab-5b93-a888-b86e89c27d0f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{L3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309279} {:answer/id #uuid "9e1acb02-1114-509d-910a-98a42188ebbd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{L1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310024}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{L3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309279} :answer-field/id #uuid "0676014f-804f-59e5-bdff-81ae06e0bea9" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310811} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1323f90a-02bd-56b9-8366-20c0593acd49" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "evaluating at $t=0$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308885} {:answer/id #uuid "3302abb0-2676-5e15-8a5e-e973064f4863" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "differentiating and using the sum rule" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309136} {:answer/id #uuid "5f4876b5-f5b7-5c5b-b070-7fabe22ebc4f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "multiplying both sides by ${e}^{At}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309463} {:answer/id #uuid "6a8dd418-5f24-589e-bdee-aad054a11f19" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "applying a change of variables" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309576}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "evaluating at $t=0$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308885} :answer-field/id #uuid "26b02ba4-09b1-554e-bc7e-4214b48c445f" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310889} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "89378a2d-4acc-5784-bc7b-ecf07978d854" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "applying a change of variables" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309828} {:answer/id #uuid "9af06cd8-24db-5a45-96c2-35845daedc0b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "substituting ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+g(t)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310001} {:answer/id #uuid "b46a0660-6e5d-5316-9901-267efc99e277" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "evaluating at $t=0$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310209} {:answer/id #uuid "d09ffa81-f739-5099-a822-57634e2ce021" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "differentiating and using the product rule" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310425}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "substituting ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+g(t)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310001} :answer-field/id #uuid "2debb7d1-7e39-57b4-b320-31d7584ebebc" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #e