from line\n{{field-2}}\nby integrating both sides from $0$ to \n{{field-3}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L5}$ follows from line $\\text{L1}$ by  \n{{field-4}}." :question/worked-solution "Let's justify each of the selected steps.\n\n- We first consider lines $\\text{L2}$ and $\\text{L3}.$ Starting from\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}(t)=-A{e}^{-At}x(t)+{e}^{-At}{x}^{′}(t)\n$$\n\nin $\\text{L2}$ and substituting ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+g(t)$ from the original system gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}(t) & =-A{e}^{-At}x(t)+{e}^{-At}(Ax(t)+g(t)) \\\\  & =-A{e}^{-At}x(t)+A{e}^{-At}x(t)+{e}^{-At}g(t) \\\\  & ={e}^{-At}g(t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, $\\text{L3}$ follows from $\\text{L2}$ by $\\text{substituting }{x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+g(t).$\n\n- Next, we consider lines $\\text{L3}$ and $\\text{L4}.$ Integrating ${y}^{′}(t)={e}^{-At}g(t)$ from $0$ to $t$ in $\\text{L3}$ yields\n\n$$\ny(t)-y(0)={\\int }_{0}^{t}{e}^{-As}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s.\n$$\n\nSo, $\\text{L4}$ follows from $\\text{L3}$ by integrating both sides from $0$ to $t.$\n\n- Finally, we consider lines $\\text{L1}$ and $\\text{L5}.$ Evaluating $y(t)={e}^{-At}x(t)$ at $t=0$ gives\n\n$$\ny(0)={e}^{-A\\cdot 0}x(0)=Ix(0)=x(0).\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\text{L5}$ follows from $\\text{L1}$ by $\\text{evaluating at }t=0.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186311585 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8628d7e9-a768-5d12-837c-9f8ec5975e1c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "substituting ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+g(t)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309796} {:answer/id #uuid "cbc30420-63d3-5a20-aca9-244b0f999086" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "differentiating and using the product rule" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310381} {:answer/id #uuid "d3937f89-bc40-5268-a944-4ae27e48a756" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "evaluating at $t=0$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310452} {:answer/id #uuid "f4bbabed-8ca7-5ae8-84c8-fa65d6c477aa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "applyin