swer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{L3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396790} {:answer/id #uuid "4fb7fb5b-f4f6-55a9-8057-b2b401444da8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{L5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396791}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{L4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396789} :answer-field/id #uuid "41a55de6-34d3-58e7-8fef-7488002a7430" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396787}] :question/id #uuid "d73d6273-7a31-5998-90dd-91a300f07c9c" :question/math-academy-id "q-335422" :question/problem "Consider the inhomogeneous system  ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+g(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix. A derivation of the formula for the solution $x(t)$ passing through $x({t}_{0})$ is presented below.\n\n$\\text{L1}:\\,$ Let $y(t)={e}^{-A(t-{t}_{0})}x(t)$  \n\n$\\text{L2}:\\,$ ${y}^{′}(t)=-A{e}^{-A(t-{t}_{0})}x(t)+{e}^{-A(t-{t}_{0})}{x}^{′}(t)$  \n\n$\\text{L3}:\\,$ ${y}^{′}(t)={e}^{-A(t-{t}_{0})}g(t)$  \n\n$\\text{L4}:\\,$ $y(t)-y({t}_{0})={\\int }_{{t}_{0}}^{t}{e}^{-A(s-{t}_{0})}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s$\n\n$\\text{L5}:\\,$ $y({t}_{0})=x({t}_{0})$ \n\n$\\text{L6}:\\,$ $y(t)=x({t}_{0})+{\\int }_{{t}_{0}}^{t}{e}^{-A(s-{t}_{0})}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s$  \n\n$\\text{L7}:\\,$ ${e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}y(t)={e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}x({t}_{0})+{\\int }_{{t}_{0}}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s$\n\n$\\text{L8}:\\,$ ${e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}y(t)=x(t)$\n\n$\\text{L9}:\\,$ $x(t)={e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}x({t}_{0})+{\\int }_{{t}_{0}}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s$\n\nSelect the correct options to justify each step of the reasoning.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L2}$ follows from $\\text{L1}$ by  \n{{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L6}$ follows from line\n{{field-2}}\nby substituting \n{{field-3}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L7}$ follows from line $\\text{L6}$ by  \n{{field-4}}." :question/worked-solution "Let's justify each of the selected steps.\n\n- We first consider lines $\\text{L1}$ and $\\text{L2}.$ Differentiating $y(t)={e}^{-A(t-{t}_{0})}x(t)$ and applying the product rule gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}(t) & =({e}^{-A(t-{t}_{0})})^{′}x(t)+{e}^{-A(t-{t}_{0})}{x}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =(-A){e}^{-A(t-{t}_{0})}x(t)+{e}^{-A(t-{t}_{0})}{x}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =-A{e}^{-A(t-{t}_{0})}x(t)+{e}^{-A(t-{t}_{0})}{x}^{′}(t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, $\\text{L2}$ follows from $\\text{L1}$ by $\\text{differentiating and using the product rule}.$\n\n- Next, we consider lines $\\text{L4}$, $\\text{L5}$, and $\\text{L6}.$ From $\\text{L4}$ we have\n\n$$\ny(t)-y({t}_{0})={\\int }_{{t}_{0}}^{t}{e}^{-A(s-{t}_{0})}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s.\n$$\n\nUsing $y({t}_{0})=x({t}_{0})$ from $\\text{L5}$, this becomes\n\n$$\ny(t)-x({t}_{0})={\\int }_{{t}_{0}}^{t}{e}^{-A(s-{t}_{0})}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s,\n$$\n\nso\n\n$$\ny(t)=x({t}_{0})+{\\int }_{{t}_{0}}^{t}{e}^{-A(s-{t}_{0})}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s.\n$$\n\nThus, $\\text{L6}$ follows from $\\text{L4}$ by substituting $y({t}_{0})=x({t}_{0}).$\n\n- Finally, we consider lines $\\text{L6}$ and $\\text{L7}.$ Multiplying both sides of\n\n$$\ny(t)=x({t}_{0})+{\\int }_{{t}_{0}}^{t}{e}^{-A(s-{t}_{0})}g(s)\\,ds\n$$\n\nfrom $\\text{L6}$ by ${e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}y(t) & ={e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}x({t}_{0})+{e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}{\\int }_{{t}_{0}}^{t}{e}^{-A(s-{t}_{0})}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s \\\\  & ={e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}x({t}_{0})+{\\int }_{{t}_{0}}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\text{L7}$ follows from $\\text{L6}$ by $\\text{multiplying both sides by }{e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186479869 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a54c25f2-ec7a-5f45-8333-64894e9c36b8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "multiplying both sides by ${e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186479606} {:answer/id #uuid "e6ee81f1-cc2e-5a93-bc97-94e6da94d3da" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "integrating both sides" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186479700} {:answer/id #uuid "fdcdd330-e92b-53ae-8aeb-507434e360ba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "evaluating at $t={t}_{0}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186479741} {:answer/id #uuid "fe0eff0a-240e-5a8f-b8f7-fcab48d77834" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "multiplying both sides by ${e}^{A(t+{t}_{0})}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186479742}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "multiplying both sides by ${e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186479606} :answer-field/id #uuid "99e629b7-39a5-51b6-b459-757a403eb36a" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186479792} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "00fc88d9-c967-5bb7-b451-454260604f2c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "substituting ${e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}y(t)=x(t)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186479359} {:answer/id #uuid "2039df82-473f-56ad-9c29-29e56eabeb40" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "multiplying both sides by ${e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186479413} {:answer/id #uuid "a97267af-ad5a-5f52-b176-36b08839336a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "substituting ${e}^{A(t+{t}_{0})}y(t)=x(t)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186479611} {:answer/id #uuid "be6bd4f1-120c-5ac9-a950-ea25545bcc99" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "evaluating at $t={t}_{0}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186479645}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "substituting ${e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}y(t)=x(t)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186479359} :answer-field/id #uuid "c2386d4b-3d22-5cfa-bad2-0a9fcf385ddb" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186479801} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "84da5009-d69f-591d-a768-f1d70476d3d1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "substituting ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+g(t)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186479555} {:answer/id #uuid "a3398ce2-e079-5944-96c7-f41a322d62e2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "substituting ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+g(t)+{t}_{0}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186479604} {:answer/id #uuid "bacf772b-cf09-517d-b411-c2134e7ca39e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "differentiating and using the product rule" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186479639} {:answer/id #uuid "c97c6311-7ff9-5fbf-a138-a9f950165a53" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "applying a change of variables" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186479665}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "differentiating and using the product rule" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186479639} :answer-field/id #uuid "e0d35370-7864-50f8-9df1-556774fcf4eb" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186479811}] :question/id #uuid "87681964-b1bd-5510-b05d-db92c8b0be06" :question/math-academy-id "q-335431" :question/problem "Consider the inhomogeneous system  ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+g(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix. A derivation of the formula for the solution $x(t)$ passing through $x({t}_{0})$ is presented below.\n\n$\\text{L1}:\\,$ Let $y(t)={e}^{-A(t-{t}_{0})}x(t)$  \n\n$\\text{L2}:\\,$ ${y}^{′}(t)=-A{e}^{-A(t-{t}_{0})}x(t)+{e}^{-A(t-{t}_{0})}{x}^{′}(t)$  \n\n$\\text{L3}:\\,$ ${y}^{′}(t)={e}^{-A(t-{t}_{0})}g(t)$  \n\n$\\text{L4}:\\,$ $y(t)-y({t}_{0})={\\int }_{{t}_{0}}^{t}{e}^{-A(s-{t}_{0})}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s$\n\n$\\text{L5}:\\,$ $y({t}_{0})=x({t}_{0})$ \n\n$\\text{L6}:\\,$ $y(t)=x({t}_{0})+{\\int }_{{t}_{0}}^{t}{e}^{-A(s-{t}_{0})}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s$  \n\n$\\text{L7}:\\,$ ${e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}y(t)={e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}x({t}_{0})+{\\int }_{{t}_{0}}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s$\n\n$\\text{L8}:\\,$ ${e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}y(t)=x(t)$\n\n$\\text{L9}:\\,$ $x(t)={e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}x({t}_{0})+{\\int }_{{t}_{0}}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s$\n\nSelect the correct options to justify each step of the reasoning.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L2}$ follows from $\\text{L1}$ by  \n{{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L7}$ follows from line $\\text{L6}$ by  \n{{field-2}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L9}$ follows from line $\\text{L7}$ by  \n{{field-3}}." :question/worked-solution "Let's justify each of the selected steps.\n\n- We first consider lines $\\text{L1}$ and $\\text{L2}.$ Differentiating $y(t)={e}^{-A(t-{t}_{0})}x(t)$ and applying the product rule gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}(t) & =({e}^{-A(t-{t}_{0})})^{′}x(t)+{e}^{-A(t-{t}_{0})}{x}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =(-A){e}^{-A(t-{t}_{0})}x(t)+{e}^{-A(t-{t}_{0})}{x}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =-A{e}^{-A(t-{t}_{0})}x(t)+{e}^{-A(t-{t}_{0})}{x}^{′}(t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, $\\text{L2}$ follows from $\\text{L1}$ by $\\text{differentiating and using the product rule}.$\n\n- Next, we consider lines $\\text{L6}$ and $\\text{L7}.$ Multiplying both sides of\n\n$$\ny(t)=x({t}_{0})+{\\int }_{{t}_{0}}^{t}{e}^{-A(s-{t}_{0})}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s\n$$\n\nfrom $\\text{L6}$ by ${e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}y(t) & ={e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}x({t}_{0})+{e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}{\\int }_{{t}_{0}}^{t}{e}^{-A(s-{t}_{0})}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s \\\\  & ={e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}x({t}_{0})+{\\int }_{{t}_{0}}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\text{L7}$ follows from $\\text{L6}$ by $\\text{multiplying both sides by }{e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}.$\n\n- Finally, we consider lines $\\text{L7}$, $\\text{L8}$, and $\\text{L9}.$ From $\\text{L8}$ we know that\n\n$$\n{e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}y(t)=x(t).\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}y(t)=x(t)$ into\n\n$$\n{e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}y(t)={e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}x({t}_{0})+{\\int }_{{t}_{0}}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s\n$$\n\nfrom $\\text{L7}$ gives\n\n$$\nx(t)={e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}x({t}_{0})+{\\int }_{{t}_{0}}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\text{L9}$ follows from $\\text{L7}$ by $\\text{substituting }{e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}y(t)=x(t).$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186535981 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "42b3ed5c-fad2-5cc4-8d0b-6a6baccca373" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "multiplying both sides by ${e}^{At}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186535537} {:answer/id #uuid "80c6f160-e91a-566a-bbbc-ef9f781ae2c6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "applying a change of variables" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186535638} {:answer/id #uuid "b43d995f-de71-5c35-a7e4-7783c88a1a2a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "integrating both sides" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186535711} {:answer/id #uuid "c752c0eb-512f-538b-978e-3d7df287dd00" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "evaluating at $t=0$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186535734}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "multiplying both sides by ${e}^{At}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186535537} :answer-field/id #uuid "070b8c00-5b6b-5a44-a8d1-5e51fc41aa76" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186535834} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0a8dbdd8-8dfd-5db1-b4cd-9bab37d71d9b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "multiplying both sides by ${e}^{At}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186535453} {:answer/id #uuid "55d4713b-294f-5d25-89d5-a2f64e40b04a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "evaluating at $t=0$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186535570} {:answer/id #uuid "68e03ce5-612b-5030-b312-5b4ab7a5ec29" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "differentiating and using the sum rule" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186535600} {:answer/id #uuid "864e8d51-dded-5420-af14-e1f984c4c0a7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "applying a change of variables" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186535649}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "evaluating at $t=0$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186535570} :answer-field/id #uuid "bdcdafbc-2a00-5bc3-a5dd-993258a4e62f" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186535904} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4be10430-59d1-599e-b689-c9308f9eceb6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "differentiating and using the product rule" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186535546} {:answer/id #uuid "4c3b2da4-577b-58b9-8f03-aec6ff89a8b7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "applying a change of variables" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186535547} {:answer/id #uuid "8912a77d-a8a2-5b0f-90ee-99de77bd7394" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "substituting ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+g(t)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186535653} {:answer/id #uuid "eda14cbf-71c6-5101-91f3-6c716e888eef" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "evaluating at $t=0$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186535801}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "differentiating and using the product rule" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186535546} :answer-field/id #uuid "f1dc9399-c403-56eb-8f48-08331960ca43" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186535919}] :question/id #uuid "ace7005c-d6c8-5219-91cc-32f47feb4972" :question/math-academy-id "q-335403" :question/problem "Consider the inhomogeneous system  ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+g(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix. A derivation of the formula for the solution $x(t)$ passing through $x(0)$ is presented below.\n\n$\\text{L1}:\\,$ Let $y(t)={e}^{-At}x(t)$  \n\n$\\text{L2}:\\,$ ${y}^{′}(t)=-A{e}^{-At}x(t)+{e}^{-At}{x}^{′}(t)$  \n\n$\\text{L3}:\\,$ ${y}^{′}(t)={e}^{-At}g(t)$  \n\n$\\text{L4}:\\,$ $y(t)-y(0)={\\int }_{0}^{t}{e}^{-As}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s$\n\n$\\text{L5}:\\,$ $y(0)=x(0)$ \n\n$\\text{L6}:\\,$ $y(t)=x(0)+{\\int }_{0}^{t}{e}^{-As}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s$  \n\n$\\text{L7}:\\,$ ${e}^{At}y(t)={e}^{At}x(0)+{\\int }_{0}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s$\n\n$\\text{L8}:\\,$ ${e}^{At}y(t)=x(t)$\n\n$\\text{L9}:\\,$ $x(t)={e}^{At}x(0)+{\\int }_{0}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s$\n\nSelect the correct options to justify each step of the reasoning.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L2}$ follows from $\\text{L1}$ by  \n{{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L5}$ follows from line $\\text{L1}$ by  \n{{field-2}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L7}$ follows from line $\\text{L6}$ by  \n{{field-3}}." :question/worked-solution "Let's justify each of the selected steps.\n\n- We first consider lines $\\text{L1}$ and $\\text{L2}.$ Differentiating $y(t)={e}^{-At}x(t)$ and applying the product rule gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}(t) & =({e}^{-At})^{′}x(t)+{e}^{-At}{x}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =(-A){e}^{-At}x(t)+{e}^{-At}{x}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =-A{e}^{-At}x(t)+{e}^{-At}{x}^{′}(t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, $\\text{L2}$ follows from $\\text{L1}$ by $\\text{differentiating and using the product rule}.$\n\n- Next, we consider lines $\\text{L1}$ and $\\text{L5}.$ Evaluating $y(t)={e}^{-At}x(t)$ at $t=0$ gives\n\n$$\ny(0)={e}^{-A\\cdot 0}x(0)=Ix(0)=x(0).\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\text{L5}$ follows from $\\text{L1}$ by $\\text{evaluating at }t=0.$\n\n- Finally, we consider lines $\\text{L6}$ and $\\text{L7}.$ Multiplying both sides of\n\n$$\ny(t)=x(0)+{\\int }_{0}^{t}{e}^{-As}g(s)\\,ds\n$$\n\nfrom $\\text{L6}$ by ${e}^{At}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{At}y(t) & ={e}^{At}x(0)+{e}^{At}{\\int }_{0}^{t}{e}^{-As}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s \\\\  & ={e}^{At}x(0)+{\\int }_{0}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\text{L7}$ follows from $\\text{L6}$ by $\\text{multiplying both sides by }{e}^{At}.$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Proving the Matrix Exponential Formula for IVP Solution of an Inhomogeneous System"}] :topic/math-academy-id 6691 :topic/title "Solving Inhomogeneous Systems of ODEs Using Matrix Methods"}]}
